#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:660
msgid "Uploading Data"
msgstr "Prenašanje podatkov"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:662
msgid ""
"Once the above CSV files are ready, you can run the analysis using OSCAR, "
"which will generate a summary report you can use either for eco-"
"certification or for your own data-driven purposes. In the `OSCAR` "
"interface, note the following:"
msgstr ""
"Ko so zgornje datoteke CSV pripravljene, lahko zaženete analizo z uporabo "
"programa OSCAR, ki bo ustvaril povzetek poročila, ki ga lahko uporabite za "
"okoljsko certificiranje ali za lastne namene, ki temeljijo na podatkih. V "
"vmesniku `OSCAR` upoštevajte naslednje:"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:664
msgid ""
"The interface language is currently German only; see below for translations."
msgstr "Jezik vmesnika je trenutno samo nemščina; za prevode glejte spodaj."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:666
msgid "The duration of the measurements in seconds must be specified."
msgstr "Določiti je treba trajanje meritev v sekundah."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:668
msgid "A semicolon separator is used."
msgstr "Uporabiti je treba ločilo s podpičjem."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:670
msgid ""
"The correct formatting of the time stamp must be specified for each of the "
"uploaded files, e.g.,`%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%OS`."
msgstr ""
"Za vsako od naloženih datotek je treba določiti pravilno oblikovanje "
"časovnega žiga, npr. `%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%OS`."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:672
msgid "Step 1: Obtain Measurement Data"
msgstr "1. korak: Pridobitev izmerjenih podatkov"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:674
msgid ""
"The landing page of the website (below) states that the first step is "
"obtaining measurement data (German: *Erfassung Messdaten*). If you are at "
"this point in the process, you should have already measured your software "
"and prepared the CSV files."
msgstr ""
"Ciljna stran spletnega mesta (spodaj) navaja, da je prvi korak pridobitev "
"izmerjenih podatkov (nemško: *Erfassung Messdaten*). Če ste na tej točki "
"postopka, bi morali že izmeriti svojo programsko opremo in pripraviti "
"datoteke CSV."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:676
msgid ""
"![First obtain the measurement data (German: *Erfassung Messdaten*) in a "
"laboratory.](images/sec3_oscar_1_landing.png)"
msgstr ""
"![Najprej pridobite podatke meritev (nemško: *Erfassung Messdaten*) v "
"laboratoriju.](images/sec3_oscar_1_landing.png)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:678
msgid ""
"All examples here are based on the Okular data in [this ZIP file](https://"
"invent.kde.org/teams/eco/feep/-/blob/master/measurements/"
"okular/2022-09-22/2022-okular-data.zip)."
msgstr ""
"Vsi primeri tukaj temeljijo na podatkih Okularja v [tej datoteki ZIP]"
"(https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/feep/-/blob/master/measurements/"
"okular/2022-09-22/2022-okular-data.zip)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:680
msgid "Step 2: Upload Measurement Data"
msgstr "2. korak: Prenos podatkov meritev"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:682
msgid ""
"Once you have the CSV files for the baseline, idle mode, and standard usage "
"scenario measurements ready, click on *(2) Upload Messdaten* > *Upload*."
msgstr ""
"Ko imate pripravljene datoteke CSV za meritve osnovnega stanja, stanja "
"mirovanja in standardnega scenarija uporabe, kliknite *(2) Upload Messdaten* "
"> *Upload*."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:684
msgid ""
"The measurement data (German: *Messdaten*) include the log file of actions "
"(German: *Aktionen*), energy consumption (German: *Elektrische Leistung*), "
"and hardware performance data (German: *Hardware-Auslastung*)."
msgstr ""
"Podatki meritev (nemško: *Messdaten*) vključujejo datoteko dnevnika dejanj "
"(nemško: *Aktionen*), porabe energije (nemško: *Elektrische Leistung*) in "
"podatkov o delovanju strojne opreme (nemško: *Hardware-Auslastung*)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:686
msgid ""
"Under *Messungen*, upload either the idle mode or standard usage scenario "
"measurement data."
msgstr ""
"V razdelku *Messungen* prenesite podatke meritev stanja mirovanja ali "
"standardnega scenarija uporabe."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:688
msgid ""
"For *Art der Messung* (‘Type of Measurement’) in the lower right of the UX, "
"select *Leerlauf* (‘Idle Mode’) or *Nutzungsszenario* (‘Usage Scenario’) "
"depending on which report you wish to generate."
msgstr ""
"Navedite trajanje scenarijev meritev v sekundah (nemško: *Dauer der "
"Einzelmessungen (s)*)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:690
msgid "Under *Baselines* upload the baseline measurement data."
msgstr ""
"Upoštevajte, da se osnovne meritve vedno prenesejo skupaj z meritvami v "
"stanju mirovanja ali standardnem scenariju uporabe."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:692
msgid ""
"Indicate the duration of the measurement scenarios in seconds (German: "
"*Dauer der Einzelmessungen (s)*)."
msgstr ""
"Navedite trajanje merilnih scenarijev v sekundah (nemško: *Dauer der "
"Einzelmessungen (s)*)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:694
msgid ""
"Note that the baseline measurements are always uploaded along with either "
"the idle mode or standard usage scenario measurements."
msgstr ""
"Upoštevajte, da se osnovne meritve vedno naložijo skupaj z meritvami v "
"stanju mirovanja ali standardnem scenariju uporabe."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:696
msgid ""
"See below for what a completed upload for the *Nutzungsszenario* looks like."
msgstr ""
"Spodaj si lahko ogledate, kako je videti dokončan prenos za "
"*Nutzungssscenario*."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:698
msgid ""
"![Uploading the measurement data (German: *Upload Messdaten*).](images/"
"sec3_oscar_2_upload.png)"
msgstr ""
"![Prenos podatkov meritev (nemško: *Upload Messdaten*).](images/"
"sec3_oscar_2_upload.png)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:700
msgid ""
"***Timestamps*** &nbsp;&nbsp; Once the data has been uploaded, you will need "
"to tell `OSCAR` how to read the data."
msgstr ""
"***Časovni žigi*** Ko so podatki preneseni, boste morali `OSCAR`ju` "
"povedati, kako naj jih prebere."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:702
msgid ""
"Let’s start with the timestamp format (German: *Formatierung Zeitstempel*). "
"This is one aspect of the process which can cause problems if not done "
"correctly. This is done under *(2) Upload Messdaten* > *Formatierung "
"Zeitstempel*."
msgstr ""
"Začnimo s formatom časovnega žiga (nemško: *Formatierung Zeitstempel*). To "
"je en vidik postopka, ki lahko povzroči težave, če ni izveden pravilno. To "
"storite v razdelku *(2) Upload Messdaten* > *Formatierung Zeitstempel*."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:704
msgid "Consider the Okular data:"
msgstr "Razmislite o podatkih Okularja:"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:706
msgid ""
"For the log file of actions, the datetime is encoded as *YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:"
"SS* (e.g., \"2022-10-04 12:32:43.656\" in “okularActions.csv”)."
msgstr ""
"Za dnevniško datoteko dejanj je datum in čas kodiran kot *YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:"
"SS* (npr. \"2022-10-04 12:32:43.656\" v \"okularActions.csv\")."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:708
msgid ""
"In `OSCAR`, this is specified as \"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%OS\" (see screenshot "
"below). OSCAR will take care of the fractional seconds."
msgstr ""
"V `OSCAR` je to določeno kot \"%Y-%m-%d %H:%M:%OS\" (glejte spodnji posnetek "
"zaslona). OSCAR bo poskrbel za delčke sekunde."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:710
msgid ""
"For the energy consumption data, the datetime is encoded as *DD.MM.YY, HH:MM:"
"SS* (e.g., \"04.10.22, 12:32:43\" in “okular_baseline_eletrLeistung.csv”). "
"Note the period in the date and the comma seperating date from time, as well "
"as only having two digits for the year."
msgstr ""
"Za podatke o porabi energije je datum in čas kodiran kot *DD.MM.YY, HH:MM:"
"SS* (npr. \"04.10.22, 12:32:43\" v \"okular_baseline_eletrLeistung.csv\"). "
"Upoštevajte piko v datumu in vejico, ki ločuje datum od časa, ter samo dve "
"števki za leto."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:712
msgid ""
"In `OSCAR` this is specified as \"%d.%m.%y, %H:%M:%OS\" (see screenshot "
"below), in which the lowercase “%y” indicates a year with two digits."
msgstr ""
"V `OSCAR` je to določeno kot \"%d.%m.%y, %H:%M:%OS\" (glejte spodnji "
"posnetek zaslona), kjer mala črka »%y« označuje leto z dvema števkama."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:714
msgid ""
"For the hardware performance data, the datetime is encoded as *DD.MM.YYYY HH:"
"MM:SS* (e.g., \"04.10.2022 12:31:43\" in “baseline_hardware_formatiert."
"csv”). Note the period in the date and the four-digit year."
msgstr ""
"Za podatke o zmogljivosti strojne opreme je datum in čas kodiran kot *DD.MM."
"YYYY HH:MM:SS* (npr. »04.10.2022 12:31:43« v »baseline_hardware_formatiert."
"csv«). Upoštevajte piko v datumu in štirimestno leto."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:716
msgid ""
"In `OSCAR`, this is specified as: \"%d.%m.%Y %H:%M:%OS\" (see screenshot "
"below), in which the uppercase “%Y” indicates a year with four digits."
msgstr ""
"V `OSCAR` je to določeno kot: \"%d.%m.%Y %H:%M:%OS\" (glejte spodnji "
"posnetek zaslona), kjer velika črka »%Y« označuje leto s štirimi števkami."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:718
msgid ""
"![Specifying the format of the timestamps (German: *Formatierung "
"Zeitstempel*).](images/sec3_oscar_3_timestamp.png)"
msgstr ""
"![Določanje oblike časovnih žigov (nemško: *Formatierung Zeitstempel*).]"
"(images/sec3_oscar_3_timestamp.png)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:720
msgid ""
"***Measurement Data*** &nbsp;&nbsp; After the timestamps have been correctly "
"specified, let’s explore the format of the measurement data (German: "
"*Formatierung Messdaten*) in `OSCAR`."
msgstr ""
"***Podatki meritev*** Ko so časovni žigi pravilno določeni, si oglejmo "
"obliko oblike podatkov meritev (nemško: *Formatierung Messdaten*) v `OSCAR`."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:722
msgid ""
"First, take a look at the log file of actions (German: *Aktionen*). This is "
"done under *(2) Upload Messdaten* > *Formatierung Messdaten* > *Aktionen*."
msgstr ""
"Najprej si oglejmo datoteko dnevnika dejanj (nemško: *Aktionen*). To storite "
"v razdelku *(2) Upload Messdaten* > *Formatierung Messdaten* > *Aktionen*."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:724
msgid ""
"Here you need to indicate for the uploaded CSV file the separator (German: "
"*Trennzeichen*), the string delimiter (German: *Textqualifizierer*), and the "
"decimal separator (German: *Dezimaltrennzeichen*)."
msgstr ""
"Tukaj morate za naloženo datoteko CSV določiti ločilo (nemško: "
"*Trennzeichen*), ločilo nizov (nemško: *Textqualifizierer*) in decimalno "
"ločilo (nemško: *Dezimaltrennzeichen*)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:726
msgid ""
"For the Okular data, this is defined as a semi-colon separator, double "
"quotation string delimiter, and a period or full-stop decimal separator (see "
"screenshot below)."
msgstr ""
"Za podatke Okular je to definirano kot ločilo s podpičjem, ločilo z dvojnimi "
"narekovaji in ločilo s piko ali decimalno piko (glejte spodnji posnetek "
"zaslona)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:728
msgid "Additionally, you will need to specify the following:"
msgstr "Dodatno boste morali določiti naslednje:"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:730
msgid ""
"whether the first line contains headings (German: *Erste Zeile enthält "
"Überschriften*);"
msgstr ""
"ali prva vrstica vsebuje naslove (nemško: *Erste Zeile enthält "
"Überschriften*);"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:731
msgid ""
"the number of lines to skip (German: *Anzahl zu überspringender Zeilen*); and"
msgstr ""
"število vrstic, ki jih želite preskočiti (nemško: *Anzahl zu überspringender "
"Zeilen*); in"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:732
msgid "the character encoding (German: *Zeichensatz (Encoding)*)."
msgstr "kodiranje znakov (nemško: *Zeichensatz (Encoding)*)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:734
msgid ""
"For the Okular data, this is defined as follows in the following screenshot: "
"“first line contains headings” is unchecked, 0 lines are skipped, and "
"character encoding is utf-8."
msgstr ""
"Za podatke Okular je to na naslednjem posnetku zaslona definirano takole: "
"možnost »prva vrstica vsebuje naslove« ni označena, 0 vrstic je preskočenih "
"in kodiranje znakov je utf-8."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:736
#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:746
msgid ""
"When everything is defined correctly, a preview of the spreadsheet will be "
"shown."
msgstr "Ko je vse pravilno definirano, se bo prikazal predogled preglednice."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:738
msgid ""
"![Specifying the format of the measurement data (German: *Formatierung "
"Messdaten*) for the log file of actions (German: *Aktionen*).](images/"
"sec3_oscar_4_actions.png)"
msgstr ""
"![Določanje oblike zapisa podatkov meritev (nemško: *Formatierung "
"Messdaten*) za datoteko dnevnika dejanj (nemško: *Aktionen*).](images/"
"sec3_oscar_4_actions.png)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:740
msgid ""
"Second, take a look at the energy consumption measurements (German: "
"*Elektrische Leistung*). This is done under *(2) Upload Messdaten* > "
"*Formatierung Messdaten* > *Elektrische Leistung*."
msgstr ""
"Nato si oglejte meritve porabe energije (nemško: *Elektrische Leistung*). To "
"storite v razdelku *(2) Upload Messdaten* > *Formatierung Messdaten* > "
"*Elektrische Leistung*."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:742
msgid ""
"The required input is the same as for the log file of actions, seen in the "
"following screenshot."
msgstr ""
"Zahtevani vnos je enak kot za datoteko dnevnika dejanj, ki je prikazana na "
"naslednjem posnetku zaslona."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:744
msgid ""
"For the Okular data here, this is a semi-colon separator, double quotation "
"string delimiter, and character encoding utf-8. However, now a comma is "
"specified for the decimal separator and a checkmark indicates that the first "
"line contains headings. Finally, the 1st line is skipped."
msgstr ""
"Za podatke Okular je to tukaj ločilo s podpičjem, ločilo z dvojnimi "
"narekovaji in kodiranje znakov utf-8. Vendar je zdaj za decimalno ločilo "
"določena vejica, kljukica pa označuje, da prva vrstica vsebuje naslove. "
"Nazadnje se prva vrstica preskoči."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:748
msgid ""
"![Specifying the format for the energy consumption data (German: "
"*Elektrische Leistung*).](images/sec3_oscar_5_energy.png)"
msgstr ""
"![Določanje oblike zapisa za podatke o porabi energije (nemško: *Elektrische "
"Leistung*).](images/sec3_oscar_5_energy.png)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:750
msgid ""
"Finally, take a look at the hardware performance data (German: *Hardware-"
"Auslastung*). This is done under *(2) Upload Messdaten* > *Formatierung "
"Messdaten* > *Hardware-Auslastung*."
msgstr ""
"Na koncu si oglejte podatke o zmogljivosti strojne opreme (nemško: *Hardware-"
"Auslastung*). To storite v *(2) Upload Messdaten* > *Formatierung Messdaten* "
"> *Hardware-Auslastung*."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:752
msgid ""
"The required input is the same. The input in this example is a semi-colon "
"separator, a double quotation string delimiter, a period (a.k.a. full stop) "
"decimal separator. There is a checkmark that the first line contains "
"headings, 0 lines are skipped, and the character encoding is utf-8."
msgstr ""
"Zahtevani vnos je enak. Vnos v tem primeru je ločilo s podpičjem, ločilo z "
"dvojnimi narekovaji in decimalno ločilo s piko. Obstaja kljukica, ki "
"označuje, da prva vrstica vsebuje naslove, 0 vrstic je preskočenih in "
"kodiranje znakov je utf-8."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:754
msgid ""
"However, now there is the additional requirement of specifying the columns "
"(German: *Spalten*)."
msgstr ""
"Vendar pa je zdaj potrebna dodatna zahteva po določitvi stolpcev (nemško: "
"*Spalten*)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:756
msgid ""
"For the columns specification, the following need to be identified; select "
"NA for unused columns, e.g., “Auslastung Auslagerungsdatei” here."
msgstr ""
"Za specifikacijo stolpcev je treba določiti naslednje; za neuporabljene "
"stolpce izberite NA, npr. tukaj »Auslastung Auslagerungsdatei«."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:758
msgid "*Zeitstempel*: Datetime (i.e., ‘Date-Time’)"
msgstr "*Zeitstempel*: Datetime (i.e., ‘Date-Time’)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:759
msgid "*CPU-Auslastung*: CPU (i.e., ‘X.CPU.Totl’)"
msgstr "*CPU-Auslastung*: CPU (i.e., ‘X.CPU.Totl’)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:760
msgid "*RAM-Auslastung*: RAM (i.e., ‘X.MEM.Used’)"
msgstr "*RAM-Auslastung*: RAM (i.e., ‘X.MEM.Used’)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:761
msgid "*Über Netzwerk gesendet*: Network transmitted (i.e., ‘X.NET.TxKBTot’)"
msgstr "*Über Netzwerk gesendet*: Network transmitted (i.e., ‘X.NET.TxKBTot’)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:762
msgid "*Über Netzwerk empfangen*: Network received (i.e., ‘X.NET.RxKBTot’)"
msgstr "*Über Netzwerk empfangen*: Network received (i.e., ‘X.NET.RxKBTot’)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:763
msgid "*Von Festplatte gelesen*: Disk read (i.e., ‘X.DSK.ReadKBTot’)"
msgstr "*Von Festplatte gelesen*: Disk read (i.e., ‘X.DSK.ReadKBTot’)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:764
msgid "*Auf Festplatte geschrieben*: Disk written (i.e., ‘X.DSK.WriteKBTot’)"
msgstr "*Auf Festplatte geschrieben*: Disk written (i.e., ‘X.DSK.WriteKBTot’)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:765
msgid "*Auslastung Auslagerungsdatei*: Swap (here, ‘N/A’)"
msgstr "*Auslastung Auslagerungsdatei*: Swap (here, ‘N/A’)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:767
msgid ""
"![Specifying the format for the hardware performance data (German: *Hardware-"
"Auslastung*).](images/sec3_oscar_6_hw.png)"
msgstr ""
"![Določanje oblike zapisa za podatke o zmogljivosti strojne opreme (nemško: "
"*Hardware-Auslastung*).](images/sec3_oscar_6_hw.png)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:769
msgid "Translations"
msgstr "Prevodi"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:771
msgid ""
"Here is an overview of some of the German terminology used in `OSCAR` and "
"the English translations:"
msgstr ""
"Tukaj je pregled nekaterih nemških izrazov, uporabljenih v `OSCAR`ju in "
"angleških prevodih:"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:773
msgid "*Messungen*: Measurements (e.g., Idle Mode or SUS)"
msgstr "*Messungen*: Measurements (e.g., Idle Mode or SUS)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:774
msgid "*Aktionen*: Actions (i.e., log file of actions taken)"
msgstr "*Aktionen*: Actions (i.e., log file of actions taken)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:775
msgid ""
"*Elektrische Leistung*: ‘Electrical power’ (i.e., energy consumption "
"measurements)"
msgstr ""
"*Elektrische Leistung*: ‘Electrical power’ (i.e., energy consumption "
"measurements)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:776
msgid ""
"*Hardware-Auslastung*: ‘Hardware load’ (i.e., hardware performance "
"measurements)"
msgstr ""
"*Hardware-Auslastung*: ‘Hardware load’ (i.e., hardware performance "
"measurements)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:777
msgid ""
"*Dauer der Einzelmessungen (s)*: ‘Duration of the individual measurements "
"(s)’ (i.e., specify how long each iteration was in seconds)"
msgstr ""
"*Dauer der Einzelmessungen (s)*: ‘Duration of the individual measurements "
"(s)’ (i.e., specify how long each iteration was in seconds)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:778
msgid "*Art der Messung*: ‘Type of measurement’"
msgstr "*Art der Messung*: ‘Type of measurement’"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:779
msgid "*Leerlauf*: ‘Idle’ (i.e., Idle mode)"
msgstr "*Leerlauf*: ‘Idle’ (i.e., Idle mode)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:780
msgid "*Nutzungsszenario*: ‘Usage scenario’ (i.e., SUS)"
msgstr "*Nutzungsszenario*: ‘Usage scenario’ (i.e., SUS)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:782
msgid "*Formatierung Messdaten*: ‘Formatting measurement data’"
msgstr "*Formatierung Messdaten*: ‘Formatting measurement data’"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:783
msgid "*Formatierung Zeitstempel*: ‘Formatting timestamp’"
msgstr "*Formatierung Zeitstempel*: ‘Formatting timestamp’"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:785
msgid "*Trennzeichen* ‘Separator’"
msgstr "*Trennzeichen* ‘Separator’"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:786
msgid "*Textqualifizierer*: ‘String delimiter’"
msgstr "*Textqualifizierer*: ‘String delimiter’"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:787
msgid "*Dezimaltrennzeichen*: ‘Decimal separator’"
msgstr "*Dezimaltrennzeichen*: ‘Decimal separator’"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:788
msgid "*Erste Zeile enthält Überschriften*: ‘First line contains headings’"
msgstr "*Erste Zeile enthält Überschriften*: ‘First line contains headings’"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:789
msgid "*Anzahl zu überspringender Zeilen*: ‘Number of lines to skip’"
msgstr "*Anzahl zu überspringender Zeilen*: ‘Number of lines to skip’"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:790
msgid "*Zeichensatz (Encoding)*: ‘Character set (encoding)’"
msgstr "*Zeichensatz (Encoding)*: ‘Character set (encoding)’"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:792
msgid "*Spalten*: Columns"
msgstr "*Spalten*: Columns"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:793
msgid "*Zeitstempel*: ‘Datetime’"
msgstr "*Zeitstempel*: ‘Datetime’"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:794
msgid "*CPU-Auslastung*: ‘CPU utilization’"
msgstr "*CPU-Auslastung*: ‘CPU utilization’"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:795
msgid "*RAM-Auslastung*: ‘RAM utilization’"
msgstr "*RAM-Auslastung*: ‘RAM utilization’"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:796
msgid "*Über Netzwerk gesendet*: ‘Sent via network’"
msgstr "*Über Netzwerk gesendet*: ‘Sent via network’"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:797
msgid "*Über Netzwerk empfangen*: ‘Received via network’"
msgstr "*Über Netzwerk empfangen*: ‘Received via network’"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:798
msgid "*Von Festplatte gelesen*: ‘Read from disk’"
msgstr "*Von Festplatte gelesen*: ‘Read from disk’"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:799
msgid "*Auf Festplatte geschrieben*: ‘Written to disk’"
msgstr "*Auf Festplatte geschrieben*: ‘Written to disk’"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:800
msgid "*Auslastung Auslagerungsdatei*: ‘Swap file utlization’"
msgstr "*Auslastung Auslagerungsdatei*: ‘Swap file utlization’"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:802
msgid "Step 3: Generating The Reports (Idle, SUS)"
msgstr "3. korak: Ustvarjanje poročil (mirovanje, SUS)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:804
msgid ""
"After completing the above, the report can be generated and downloaded. You "
"will need to do this process twice, once for (i) the idle mode and (ii) "
"standard usage scenario measurements, resulting in two documents."
msgstr ""
"Po opravljenem zgornjem postopku lahko poročilo ustvarite in prenesete. Ta "
"postopek boste morali opraviti dvakrat, enkrat za (i) meritve načina "
"mirovanja in (ii) standardnega scenarija uporabe, rezultat česar sta dva "
"dokumenta."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:806
msgid ""
"![Generating the report (German: *Bericht erzeugen*).](images/"
"sec3_oscar_7_report.png)"
msgstr ""
"![Ustvarjanje poročila (nemško: *Bericht erzeugen*).](images/"
"sec3_oscar_7_report.png)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:808
msgid ""
"For Blue Angel eco-certification, the two reports will be submitted for "
"evaluation by RAL."
msgstr ""
"Za okoljski certifikat Blue Angel bosta obe poročili predloženi v oceno RAL."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:810
#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:846
msgid ""
"For examples of the above for Okular, see KDE’s [Blue Angel Applications]"
"(https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/blue-angel-application) repository:"
msgstr ""
"Za primere zgoraj navedenega za Okular glejte repozitorij [Blue Angel "
"Applications](https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/blue-angel-application) KDE:"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:812
msgid ""
"[OSCAR Report: Idle Mode](https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/blue-angel-"
"application/-/blob/master/applications/okular/de-uz-215-eng-annex-3-okular-"
"idle.pdf)"
msgstr ""
"[Poročilo OSCAR: Način mirovanja](https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/blue-"
"angel-application/-/blob/master/applications/okular/de-uz-215-eng-annex-3-"
"okular-idle.pdf)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:813
msgid ""
"[OSCAR Report: SUS](https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/blue-angel-"
"application/-/blob/master/applications/okular/de-uz-215-eng-annex-3-okular-"
"scenario.pdf)"
msgstr ""
"[Poročilo OSCAR: SUS](https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/blue-angel-"
"application/-/blob/master/applications/okular/de-uz-215-eng-annex-3-okular-"
"scenario.pdf)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:815
msgid "Preparing The Documentation For Blue Angel"
msgstr "Priprava dokumentacije za Blue Angel"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:817
msgid ""
"For Blue Angel eco-certification, it is necessary to complete several forms "
"alongside the two reports from `OSCAR`."
msgstr ""
"Za ekocertifikacijo Blue Angel je potrebno izpolniti več obrazcev poleg dveh "
"poročil `OSCAR`."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:819
msgid "Information that needs to be included in the forms is as follows:"
msgstr "Informacije, ki jih je treba vključiti v obrazce, so naslednje:"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:821
msgid ""
"Details about the software (name, version) and measurement process (when and "
"where measurements were made, etc.)."
msgstr ""
"Podrobnosti o programski opremi (ime, različica) in merilnem postopku (kdaj "
"in kje so bile opravljene meritve itd.)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:823
msgid ""
"Technical details about the power meter (instrument, sampling frequency, "
"length of scenario, sample size)."
msgstr ""
"Tehnične podrobnosti o merilniku moči (instrument, frekvenca vzorčenja, "
"dolžina scenarija, velikost vzorca)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:825
msgid ""
"Technical details about the reference system (year, model, processor, cores, "
"etc.)."
msgstr ""
"Tehnične podrobnosti o referenčnem sistemu (leto, model, procesor, jedra "
"itd.)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:827
msgid "Software stack used for the measurements (`xdotool`, `Collectl`, etc.)."
msgstr ""
"Sklad programske opreme, ki se uporablja za meritve (`xdotool`, `Collectl` "
"itd.)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:829
msgid ""
"Minimum system requirements (processor architecture, local working memory, "
"etc.)."
msgstr ""
"Minimalne sistemske zahteve (arhitektura procesorja, lokalni delovni "
"pomnilnik itd.)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:831
msgid "Energy consumption results found in the `OSCAR` reports or equivalent."
msgstr "Rezultati porabe energije v poročilih `OSCAR` ali enakovrednih."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:833
msgid ""
"Hardware utilization results, which includes the following (for IDLE use the "
"idle mode measurements, and for SUS use the standard usage scenario "
"measurements):"
msgstr ""
"Rezultati izkoriščenosti strojne opreme, ki vključujejo naslednje (za stanje "
"mirovanja uporabite meritve v stanju mirovanja, za stanje SUS pa meritve v "
"standardnem scenariju uporabe):"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:834
msgid ""
"*Full Load*: “For processing power, the full load is 100%, for working "
"memory the sum of the installed RAM capacities, for network bandwidth the "
"maximum transmission speed, etc.” (Blue Angel award criteria: p. 23)."
msgstr ""
"*Polna obremenitev*: »Za procesorsko moč je polna obremenitev 100 %, za "
"delovni pomnilnik vsota nameščenih zmogljivosti RAM-a, za pasovno širino "
"omrežja največja hitrost prenosa itd.« (merila za podelitev nagrade Blue "
"Angel: str. 23)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:835
msgid ""
"*Base Load*: Average load for the reference system in Baseline measurements."
msgstr ""
"*Osnovna obremenitev*: Povprečna obremenitev referenčnega sistema pri "
"osnovnih meritvah."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:836
msgid ""
"*Idle/SUS Load*: Average load for the reference system for IDLE/SUS "
"measurements."
msgstr ""
"*Obremenitev v stanju mirovanja/SUS*: Povprečna obremenitev referenčnega "
"sistema za meritve v stanju mirovanja/SUS."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:838
msgid ""
"From the above measurements, the following calculations are made for "
"hardware utilization (for IDLE use the idle mode measurements, and for SUS "
"use the standard usage scenario measurements):"
msgstr ""
"Iz zgornjih meritev so narejeni naslednji izračuni za izkoriščenost strojne "
"opreme (za IDLE uporabite meritve v načinu mirovanja, za SUS pa meritve v "
"standardnem scenariju uporabe):"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:839
msgid "*Net Load*: IDLE/SUS Load - Base Load"
msgstr "*Neto obremenitev*: Obremenitev IDLE/SUS - Osnovna obremenitev"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:840
msgid "*Allocation Factor*: Net Load/(Full Load - Base Load)"
msgstr ""
"*Faktor dodelitve*: Neto obremenitev/(polna obremenitev - osnovna "
"obremenitev)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:841
msgid "*Effective Load*: Net Load + Allocation Factor * Base Load"
msgstr ""
"*Efektivna obremenitev*: Neto obremenitev + Faktor dodelitve * Osnovna "
"obremenitev"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:842
msgid "*Hardware Utilization* (SUS only): Effective Load * Time (seconds)"
msgstr ""
"*Izkoriščenost strojne opreme* (samo SUS): Efektivna obremenitev * Čas "
"(sekunde)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:844
msgid ""
"For Blue Angel eco-certification, the above information will be added to two "
"documents called “Annex 1” and “Annex 2”."
msgstr ""
"Za okoljsko certificiranje Blue Angel bodo zgornje informacije dodane dvema "
"dokumentoma, imenovanima »Priloga 1« in »Priloga 2«."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:848
#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1042
msgid ""
"[Annex 1](https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/blue-angel-application/-/blob/"
"master/applications/okular/de-uz-215-eng-annex-1-okular.docx)"
msgstr ""
"[Annex 1](https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/blue-angel-application/-/blob/"
"master/applications/okular/de-uz-215-eng-annex-1-okular.docx)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:849
#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1043
msgid ""
"[Annex 2](https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/blue-angel-application/-/blob/"
"master/applications/okular/de-uz-215-eng-annex-2-okular.xlsx)"
msgstr ""
"[Annex 2](https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/blue-angel-application/-/blob/"
"master/applications/okular/de-uz-215-eng-annex-2-okular.xlsx)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:851
msgid "<a name=\"sec:gosundPM\"></a> Alternative: Gosund SP111 Setup"
msgstr "<a name=\"sec:gosundPM\"></a> Alternative: Gosund SP111 Setup"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:853
msgid ""
"Want to get started with the process of measuring your software, but short "
"on cash or gear? Want to give the process a try without setting up a "
"dedicated lab? Try this hack converting an inexpensive power plug to a power "
"meter, courtesy of Volker Krause, who also documented the process provided "
"here. You can read more at the following posts from Volker’s blog:"
msgstr ""
"Želite začeti s postopkom merjenja vaše programske opreme, vendar vam "
"primanjkuje denarja ali opreme? Želite poskusiti postopek, ne da bi morali "
"ustanoviti namenski laboratorij? Poskusite ta trik, s katerim poceni vtič "
"pretvorite v merilnik moči, ki ga je pripravil Volker Krause, ki je postopek "
"tudi dokumentiral tukaj. Več si lahko preberete v naslednjih objavah z "
"Volkerjevega bloga:"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:855
msgid ""
"[“*Cheap Electric Power Measurement*”](https://web.archive.org/"
"web/20221002125057/https://volkerkrause.eu/2020/10/17/kde-cheap-power-"
"measurement-tools.html)"
msgstr ""
"[“*Cheap Electric Power Measurement*”](https://web.archive.org/"
"web/20221002125057/https://volkerkrause.eu/2020/10/17/kde-cheap-power-"
"measurement-tools.html)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:857
msgid ""
"[“*KDE Eco Sprint July 2022*”](https://web.archive.org/web/20220819231538/"
"https://www.volkerkrause.eu/2022/07/23/kde-eco-sprint-july-2022.html)"
msgstr ""
"[“*KDE Eco Sprint July 2022*”](https://web.archive.org/web/20220819231538/"
"https://www.volkerkrause.eu/2022/07/23/kde-eco-sprint-july-2022.html)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:859
msgid ""
"Below is a guide to setting up a [Gosund SP111](https://templates.blakadder."
"com/gosund_SP111_v2.html) power plug already [flashed](https://github.com/"
"tasmota/docs/blob/development/docs/devices/BlitzWolf-SHP6.md) with [Tasmota "
"firmware](https://tasmota.github.io/docs) in 10 steps."
msgstr ""
"Spodaj je vodnik za nastavitev vtičnice [Gosund SP111](https://templates."
"blakadder.com/gosund_SP111_v2.html), ki je že [programsko opremljena]"
"(https://github.com/tasmota/docs/blob/development/docs/devices/BlitzWolf-"
"SHP6.md) z vdelano programsko opremo [Tasmota](https://tasmota.github.io/"
"docs) v 10 korakih."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:861
msgid ""
"Although the data from the inexpensive power meter will likely not be "
"accepted by the Blue Angel for eco-certification, it is nonetheless possible "
"to obtain preliminary data using this tool."
msgstr ""
"Čeprav podatki iz poceni merilnika porabe verjetno ne bodo sprejeti s strani "
"programa Blue Angel za okoljsko certificiranje, je kljub temu mogoče "
"pridobiti predhodne podatke s tem orodjem."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:863
msgid "(0) *Prerequisite*"
msgstr "(0) *Predpogoj*"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:865
msgid ""
"It is necessary to have the power plug already flashed with a sufficiently "
"new Tasmota version."
msgstr ""
"Vtičnica mora biti že programsko opremljena z dovolj novo različico programa "
"Tasmota."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:867
msgid "(1) *Firmware Reset*"
msgstr "(1) *Ponastavitev vdelane programske opreme*"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:869
msgid ""
"If the device had previously been connected to another Wifi network, it "
"might need a full reset before being able to connect to a new one."
msgstr ""
"Če je bila naprava predhodno povezana z drugim omrežjem Wi-Fi, jo bo morda "
"treba popolnoma ponastaviti, preden se bo lahko povezala z novim."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:871
msgid ""
"If the device did open a WiFi access point named “tasmota-XXXXX” this is not "
"needed, continue directly to (2)."
msgstr ""
"Če je naprava odprla dostopno točko WiFi z imenom »tasmota-XXXXX«, to ni "
"potrebno, nadaljujte neposredno z (2)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:873
msgid "Press the button for 40 seconds."
msgstr "Pritisnite gumb za 40 sekund."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:875
msgid "The device will restart and you should be able to continue at (2)."
msgstr "Naprava se bo znova zagnala in nadaljevali boste pri (2)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:877
msgid "(2) *WiFi Setup*"
msgstr "(2) *Nastavitev WiFi*"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:879
msgid ""
"The device opens a WiFi access point named “tasmota-XXXXX”&mdash;connect to "
"that."
msgstr ""
"Naprava odpre dostopno točko WiFi z imenom »tasmota-XXXXX« &mdash; povežite "
"se z njo."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:881
msgid "Open http://192.168.4.1 in a browser."
msgstr "V brskalniku odprite http://192.168.4.1."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:883
msgid ""
"The device will ask you for the WiFi name and password to connect to after "
"entering those. The device will reconnect to that WiFi and disable its "
"access point."
msgstr ""
"Naprava vas bo po vnosu imena in gesla za omrežje WiFi vprašala za povezavo. "
"Naprava se bo znova povezala s tem omrežjem WiFi in onemogočila njegovo "
"dostopno točko."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:885
msgid ""
"While doing that it should show you its new address in the browser&mdash;"
"make a note of it."
msgstr ""
"Med tem bi se moral v brskalniku prikazati njegov novi naslov &mdash; "
"zabeležite si ga."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:887
msgid ""
"In case that did not happen, check your WiFi router for the address of the "
"device."
msgstr ""
"Če se to ni zgodilo, preverite naslov naprave na svojem usmerjevalniku WiFi."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:889
msgid "(3) *Tasmota Setup*"
msgstr "(3) *Nastavitev Tasmote*"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:891
#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:917
msgid "Open the address from step (2) in a browser."
msgstr "Odprite naslov iz koraka (2) v brskalniku."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:893
msgid ""
"You should see the Tasmota web UI (a big “ON/OFF” text and a bunch of blue "
"and one red button)."
msgstr ""
"Videti bi morali spletni uporabniški vmesnik Tasmote (velik napis »VKLOP/"
"IZKLOP« in kup modrih ter en rdeč gumb)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:895
msgid "Click “Configuration”."
msgstr "Kliknite »Konfiguracija«."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:897
msgid "Click “Configure Other”."
msgstr "Kliknite »Konfiguriraj drugo«."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:899
msgid "Copy"
msgstr "Kopiraj"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:905
msgid "into the template input field."
msgstr "v polje za vnos predloge."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:907
msgid "Tick the “Activate” checkbox."
msgstr "Označite potrditveno polje »Aktiviraj«."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:909
#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:965
msgid "Click “Save”."
msgstr "Kliknite »Shrani«."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:911
msgid "The device will restart; connect to it again."
msgstr "Naprava se bo znova zagnala; ponovno se povežite z njo."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:913
msgid ""
"The UI should now also contain text fields showing electrical properties, "
"and the “Toggle” button should now actually work."
msgstr ""
"Uporabniški vmesnik bi moral zdaj vsebovati tudi besedilna polja, ki "
"prikazujejo električne lastnosti, gumb »Preklopi« pa bi moral zdaj dejansko "
"delovati."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:915
msgid "(4) *Calibration*"
msgstr "(4) *Kalibracija*"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:919
msgid ""
"Connect a purely resistive load with a known wattage, such as a conventional "
"light bulb (not a LED or energy-saving bulb)."
msgstr ""
"Priključite izključno uporovno obremenitev z znano močjo, na primer običajno "
"žarnico (ne LED ali varčno žarnico)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:921
msgid "Switch on power by clicking “Toggle” if needed."
msgstr "Po potrebi vklopite napajanje s klikom na »Preklopi«."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:923
msgid ""
"Verify that the “Power Factor” value is shown as 1 (or very close to 1); if "
"it is lower, the current load is not suited for calibration."
msgstr ""
"Preverite, ali je vrednost »Faktor moči« prikazana kot 1 (ali zelo blizu 1); "
"če je nižja, trenutna obremenitev ni primerna za kalibracijo."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:925
msgid "Click “Console”."
msgstr "Kliknite »Konzola«."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:927
msgid "Enter the following commands one at a time and press enter:"
msgstr "Vnesite naslednje ukaze enega za drugim in pritisnite enter:"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:937
msgid ""
"Enter the command PowerSet XXX with XXX replaced by the wattage specified "
"for the test load (e.g., “40” for a 40W light bulb)."
msgstr ""
"Vnesite ukaz PowerSet XXX, pri čemer XXX nadomestite z močjo, določeno za "
"testno obremenitev (npr. »40« za žarnico 40 W)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:939
msgid "Click “Main Menu”."
msgstr "Kliknite »Glavni meni«."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:941
msgid ""
"The main page now should show correct power readings with several decimals "
"precision."
msgstr ""
"Glavna stran bi morala zdaj prikazovati pravilne odčitke moči z natančnostjo "
"več decimalnih mest."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:943
msgid "(5) *MQTT Broker Setup*"
msgstr "(5) *Nastavitev posrednika MQTT*"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:945
msgid ""
"At present, the only known way to achieve high-frequency automatic readouts "
"is by polling over MQTT. This is not ideal and needs additional setup, "
"unfortunately."
msgstr ""
"Trenutno je edini znani način za doseganje visokofrekvenčnih samodejnih "
"odčitkov anketiranje MQTT. To ni idealno in žal zahteva dodatno nastavitev."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:947
msgid ""
"If you happen to have a MQTT Broker around already, skip to step (6); "
"otherwise, you need to set one up. The below scenario assumes Mosquitto is "
"packaged for your GNU/Linux distribution (and therefore does not configure "
"any security), so only do this in your own trusted network and switch it off "
"when not needed."
msgstr ""
"Če že imate posrednika MQTT, preskočite na korak (6); sicer ga morate "
"nastaviti. Spodnji scenarij predpostavlja, da je Mosquitto zapakiran za vašo "
"distribucijo GNU/Linux (in zato ne konfigurira nobene varnosti), zato to "
"storite le v svojem zaupanja vrednem omrežju in ga izklopite, ko ga ne "
"potrebujete."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:949
msgid "install the `mosquitto` package"
msgstr "namestite paket `mosquitto`"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:950
msgid ""
"add a file `/etc/mosquitto/conf.d/listen.conf` with the following content:"
msgstr ""
"dodajte datoteko `/etc/mosquitto/conf.d/listen.conf` z naslednjo vsebino:"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:955
msgid "start Mosquitto using `systemctl start mosquitto.service`"
msgstr "zaženite Mosquitto z uporabo `systemctl start mosquitto.service`"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:957
msgid "(6) *MQTT Tasmota Setup*"
msgstr "(6) *Nastavitev MQTT Tasmota*"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:959
msgid ""
"Connect to the Tasmota device using a web browser, and open the MQTT "
"configuration page via Configuration > Configure MQTT."
msgstr ""
"Povežite se z napravo Tasmota s spletnim brskalnikom in odprite "
"konfiguracijsko stran MQTT prek Configuration > Configure MQTT."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:961
msgid "Enter the IP address of the MQTT broker into the “Host” field."
msgstr "V polje “Host” vnesite IP-naslov posrednika MQTT."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:963
msgid ""
"Note down the value shown right of the “Topic” label in parentheses "
"(typically something like “tasmota_xxxxxx”). This will be needed later on to "
"address the device via MQTT. You can also change the default value to "
"something easier to remember, but this has to be unique if you have multiple "
"devices."
msgstr ""
"Zapišite si vrednost, prikazano desno od oznake “Topic” v oklepaju (običajno "
"nekaj takega kot »tasmota_xxxxxx«). To boste kasneje potrebovali za "
"naslavljanje naprave prek MQTT. Privzeto vrednost lahko spremenite tudi v "
"nekaj, kar si boste lažje zapomnili, vendar mora biti ta edinstvena, če "
"imate več naprav."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:967
msgid ""
"The device will restart and once it is back you should see output in its "
"Console prefixed with “MQT”."
msgstr ""
"Naprava se bo znova zagnala in ko bo spet vklopljena, bi morali v njeni "
"konzoli videti izpis s predpono »MQT«."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:969
msgid "(7) *Verifying MQTT Communication*"
msgstr "(7) *Preverjanje komunikacije MQTT*"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:971
msgid ""
"This assumes you have the Mosquitto client tools installed, which are "
"usually available as distribution packages."
msgstr ""
"To predvideva, da imate nameščena odjemalska orodja Mosquitto, ki so "
"običajno na voljo kot distribucijski paketi."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:973
msgid ""
"You need two terminals to verify that MQTT communication works as intended."
msgstr ""
"Potrebujete dva terminala, da preverite, ali komunikacija MQTT deluje, kot "
"je predvideno."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:975
msgid "In terminal 1, run `mosquitto_sub -t 'stat/<topic>/STATUS10'`"
msgstr "V terminalu 1 zaženite `mosquitto_sub -t 'stat/<topic>/STATUS10'`"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:976
msgid "In terminal 2, run `mosquitto_pub -t 'cmnd/<topic>/STATUS' -m '10'`"
msgstr ""
"V terminalu 2 zaženite `mosquitto_pub -t 'cmnd/<topic>/STATUS' -m '10'`"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:978
msgid "Replace `<topic>` with the value noted down in step (6)."
msgstr "Zamenjajte `<topic>` z vrednostjo, zabeleženo v koraku (6)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:980
msgid ""
"Everytime you run the second command, you should see a set of values printed "
"in the first terminal."
msgstr ""
"Vsakič, ko zaženete drugi ukaz, bi morali videti nabor vrednosti, natisnjen "
"v prvem terminalu."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:982
msgid "(8) *Continuous Power Measurements*"
msgstr "(8) *Neprekinjene meritve moči*"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:984
msgid ""
"See [these scripts](https://volkerkrause.eu/2020/10/17/kde-cheap-power-"
"measurement-tools.html)."
msgstr ""
"Oglejte si [te skripte](https://volkerkrause.eu/2020/10/17/kde-cheap-power-"
"measurement-tools.html)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:986
msgid "(9) *Switching WiFi Networks*"
msgstr "(9) *Preklapljanje omrežij WiFi*"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:988
msgid ""
"For security reasons, once connected to a WiFi network, Tasmota will not let "
"you get back to step (2) by default without hard resetting the device (40-"
"second button press). However, a hard reset also removes all settings and "
"the calibration. If you need to move to a different network, there are less "
"drastic options available, but these changes can only be made inside the "
"network you originally connected to:"
msgstr ""
"Ko se povežete z omrežjem WiFi, vam Tasmota iz varnostnih razlogov privzeto "
"ne bo dovolila, da se vrnete na korak (2) brez trde ponastavitve naprave (40-"
"sekundni pritisk na gumb). Vendar pa strojna ponastavitev odstrani tudi vse "
"nastavitve in umerjanje. Če se morate premakniti v drugo omrežje, so na "
"voljo manj drastične možnosti, vendar je te spremembe mogoče izvesti samo "
"znotraj omrežja, s katerim ste se prvotno povezali:"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:990
msgid ""
"Under Configuration > Configure WiFi, you can add details for a second WiFi "
"access point. Those will be tried alternatingly with the first configuration "
"by default. This does not compromise security, but requires you to know the "
"details for the network you want to connect to."
msgstr ""
"V razdelku Konfiguracija > Konfiguriraj WiFi lahko dodate podrobnosti za "
"drugo dostopno točko WiFi. Ti bodo privzeto preizkušeni izmenično s prvo "
"konfiguracijo. To ne ogroža varnosti, vendar zahteva, da poznate podrobnosti "
"omrežja, s katerim se želite povezati."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:992
msgid ""
"You can configure Tasmota to open an access point as in step (2) by default "
"for a minute or so after boot, and then try to connect to the known "
"configurations. This makes booting slower in known networks, and opens the "
"potential for hijacking the device, but it can be convenient when switching "
"to unknown networks. This mode can be enabled in the Console by the command "
"`WifiConfig 2`, and disabled by the command `WifiConfig 4`."
msgstr ""
"Tasmoto lahko konfigurirate tako, da privzeto odpre dostopno točko kot v "
"koraku (2) za kakšno minuto po zagonu, nato pa se poskusite povezati z "
"znanimi konfiguracijami. To povzroči počasnejši zagon v znanih omrežjih in "
"odpira možnosti za ugrabitev naprave, vendar je lahko priročno pri preklopu "
"na neznana omrežja. Ta način lahko omogočite v konzoli z ukazom `WifiConfig "
"2` in onemogočite z ukazom `WifiConfig 4`."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:994
msgid ""
"For Tasmota version 11 the 40-second button press reset can leave the device "
"in a non-booting state, whereas resetting from the Console using `Reset 1` "
"doesn’t have that problem, but has to be done before disconnecting from the "
"known WiFi as well."
msgstr ""
"Pri različici Tasmota 11 lahko ponastavitev s 40-sekundnim pritiskom gumba "
"pusti napravo v stanju brez zagona, medtem ko ponastavitev iz konzole z "
"uporabo »Ponastavi 1« nima te težave, vendar jo je treba izvesti tudi pred "
"prekinitvijo povezave z znanim WiFi."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:996
msgid "(10) *Recovering Non-Booting Devices*"
msgstr "(10) *Obnovitev nezagonskih naprav*"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:998
msgid ""
"First and foremost: **DO NOT CONNECT THE DEVICE TO MAIN POWER**! That would "
"be life-threatening. The entire flashing process is solely powered from 3.3V "
"supplied by the serial adapter. Do not do any of this without having read "
"this [getting started guide](https://tasmota.github.io/docs/Getting-"
"Started/)."
msgstr ""
"Najprej in predvsem: **NAPRAVE NE PRIKLJUČUJTE NA GLAVNO VTIČNICO**! To bi "
"bilo smrtno nevarno. Celoten postopek programiranja se napaja izključno z "
"napetostjo 3,3 V, ki jo zagotavlja serijski adapter. Ne izvajajte ničesar od "
"tega, ne da bi prebrali ta [vodnik za začetek](https://tasmota.github.io/"
"docs/Getting-Started/)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1000
msgid ""
"With Tasmota 11, you can end up in a non-booting state by merely resetting "
"the device using the 40-second button press. This does not permanently "
"damage the device, and it can be fixed with reflashing via a serial adapter."
msgstr ""
"Pri Tasmoti 11 se lahko zgodi, da se naprava ne zažene, če napravo preprosto "
"ponastavite s 40-sekundnim pritiskom na gumb. To naprave ne poškoduje trajno "
"in jo je mogoče odpraviti s ponovnim programiranjem prek serijskega "
"adapterja."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1002
msgid ""
"The basic process is described in the above [guide](https://tasmota.github."
"io/docs/Getting-Started/). The PCB layout of the Gosund SP 111 can be seen "
"[here](https://templates.blakadder.com/gosund_SP111_v1_1)."
msgstr ""
"Osnovni postopek je opisan v zgornjem [vodniku](https://tasmota.github.io/"
"docs/Getting-Started/). Postavitev tiskanega vezja Gosund SP 111 si lahko "
"ogledate [tukaj](https://templates.blakadder.com/gosund_SP111_v1_1)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1004
msgid ""
"In order for this to work, you need to connect GPIO0 (second pin on bottom "
"left in the above image) to GND **before** powering up (i.e., before "
"connecting with USB). The device LEDs (red and blue) are a useful indicator "
"of whether you ended up in the right boot mode: the red LED should be on, "
"and not flashing quickly, and the blue and red LED should not be on "
"together. Once in that state, the connection can be removed (e.g., if you "
"just hold a jumper cable to the pin) and it will remain in the right mode "
"until a reboot."
msgstr ""
"Da bi to delovalo, morate pred vklopom (tj. pred povezavo z USB) priključiti "
"GPIO0 (drugi pin spodaj levo na zgornji sliki) na GND. LED lučki naprave "
"(rdeča in modra) sta uporaben pokazatelj, ali ste se znašli v pravilnem "
"načinu zagona: rdeča LED lučka mora svetiti in ne sme hitro utripati, modra "
"in rdeča LED lučka pa ne smeta svetiti hkrati. Ko ste v tem stanju, lahko "
"povezavo odstranite (npr. če samo držite kabel za vžig) in naprava bo ostala "
"v pravilnem načinu do ponovnega zagona."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1006
msgid ""
"Again: **DO NOT CONNECT THE DEVICE TO MAIN POWER** as this is life-"
"threatening."
msgstr ""
"Še enkrat: **NE PRIKLJUČUJTE NAPRAVE NA GLAVNO NAPAJANJE**, saj je to smrtno "
"nevarno."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1008
msgid "(B) Hardware Operating Life"
msgstr "(B) Življenjska doba strojne opreme"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1010
msgid ""
"The criteria in category (B) ensure that the software has low-enough "
"performance requirements to run on older, less powerful hardware at least "
"five years old."
msgstr ""
"Merila v kategoriji (B) zagotavljajo, da ima programska oprema dovolj nizke "
"zahteve glede zmogljivosti za delovanje na starejši, manj zmogljivi strojni "
"opremi, stari vsaj pet let."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1012
msgid ""
"Many FOSS applications run on hardware much older than 5 years. In fact, "
"members of the KDE community have noted that KDE’s desktop environment "
"`Plasma` runs on hardware from even 2005!"
msgstr ""
"Številne aplikacije FOSS delujejo na strojni opremi, ki je veliko starejša "
"od 5 let. Pravzaprav so člani skupnosti KDE opazili, da KDE-jevo namizno "
"okolje `Plasma` deluje celo na strojni opremi iz leta 2005!"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1014
msgid ""
"This category is relatively easily to fulfill for the Blue Angel "
"application. Compliance entails a declaration of backward compatibility, "
"including details about the hardware on which the software runs and the "
"required software stack. To demonstrate compliance, document the following "
"information in two documents called “Annex 1” and “Annex 2”:"
msgstr ""
"To kategorijo je za aplikacijo Blue Angel relativno enostavno izpolniti. "
"Skladnost vključuje izjavo o združljivosti s prejšnjimi različicami, "
"vključno s podrobnostmi o strojni opremi, na kateri programska oprema "
"deluje, in zahtevanem programu. Za dokazovanje skladnosti dokumentirajte "
"naslednje podatke v dveh dokumentih, imenovanih »Priloga 1« in »Priloga 2«:"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1016
msgid "*Reference System Year* &mdash; e.g., 2015"
msgstr "*Reference System Year* &mdash; e.g., 2015"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1018
msgid "*Model* &mdash; e.g., Fujitsu Esprimo 920"
msgstr "*Model* &mdash; e.g., Fujitsu Esprimo 920"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1020
msgid "*Processor* &mdash; e.g., Intel Core i5-4570"
msgstr "*Processor* &mdash; e.g., Intel Core i5-4570"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1022
msgid "*Cores* &mdash; e.g., 4"
msgstr "*Cores* &mdash; e.g., 4"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1024
msgid "*Clock Speed* &mdash; e.g., 3,6 GHz"
msgstr "*Clock Speed* &mdash; e.g., 3,6 GHz"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1026
msgid "*RAM* &mdash; e.g., 4 GB"
msgstr "*RAM* &mdash; e.g., 4 GB"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1028
msgid "*Hard Disk (SSD/HDD)* &mdash; e.g., 500 GB"
msgstr "*Hard Disk (SSD/HDD)* &mdash; e.g., 500 GB"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1030
msgid "*Graphics Card* &mdash; e.g., Intel Ivybridge Desktop"
msgstr "*Graphics Card* &mdash; e.g., Intel Ivybridge Desktop"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1032
msgid "*Network* &mdash; e.g., Realtek Ethernet"
msgstr "*Network* &mdash; e.g., Realtek Ethernet"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1034
msgid "*Cache* &mdash; e.g., 6144 KB"
msgstr "*Cache* &mdash; e.g., 6144 KB"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1036
msgid "*Mainboard* &mdash; e.g., Fujitsu D3171-A1"
msgstr "*Mainboard* &mdash; e.g., Fujitsu D3171-A1"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1038
msgid "*Operating System* &mdash; e.g., Ubuntu 18.04"
msgstr "*Operating System* &mdash; e.g., Ubuntu 18.04"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1040
msgid "Again, examples for Okular can be found at the following links:"
msgstr "Primere za Okular najdete na naslednjih povezavah:"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1047
msgid ""
"As discussed in PART II, the Blue Angel user autonomy criteria cover eight "
"general areas:"
msgstr ""
"Kot je bilo razloženo v II. DELU, merila za avtonomijo uporabnikov programa "
"Blue Angel zajemajo osem splošnih področij:"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1049
msgid "Data Formats"
msgstr "Oblike podatkov"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1050
msgid "Transparency"
msgstr "Preglednost"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1051
msgid "Continuity Of Support"
msgstr "Kontinuiteta podpore"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1052
msgid "Uninstallability"
msgstr "Možnost odstranitve"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1053
msgid "Offline Capability"
msgstr "Možnost dela brez povezave"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1054
msgid "Modularity"
msgstr "Modularnost"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1055
msgid "Freedom From Advertising"
msgstr "Svoboda oglaševanja"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1056
msgid "Documentation"
msgstr "Dokumentacija"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1058
msgid ""
"Many FOSS projects may take for granted that Free Software respects user "
"autonomy and in some cases information from the above list is missing from "
"websites, manuals, wikis, etc. This may include documentation about support "
"for open standards, uninstallability, continuity of support, and so on."
msgstr ""
"Mnogi projekti FOSS lahko jemljejo za samoumevno, da prosta programska "
"oprema spoštuje avtonomijo uporabnikov, in v nekaterih primerih informacije "
"z zgornjega seznama manjkajo na spletnih mestih, v priročnikih, wikijih itd. "
"To lahko vključuje dokumentacijo o podpori za odprte standarde, možnosti "
"odstranitve, kontinuiteti podpore itd."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1060
msgid ""
"Documenting this information is important, both for fulfilling the Blue "
"Angel award criteria and for giving users information about long-term "
"sustainable use of their software and hardware."
msgstr ""
"Dokumentiranje teh informacij je pomembno tako za izpolnjevanje meril za "
"nagrado Blue Angel kot za zagotavljanje informacij uporabnikom o dolgoročni "
"trajnostni uporabi njihove programske in strojne opreme."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1062
msgid ""
"This is not an exhaustive presentation for each of the above categories of "
"the Blue Angel criteria. Rather, this guide focuses on aspects of the "
"criteria which KDE/FOSS projects can easily document and provide (which is "
"already most of the work). For the full criteria, see Section 3.1.3 in the "
"[basic award criteria](https://www.blauer-engel.de/en/productworld/resources-"
"and-energy-efficient-software-products)."
msgstr ""
"To ni izčrpna predstavitev za vsako od zgornjih kategorij meril Blue Angel. "
"Namesto tega se ta priročnik osredotoča na vidike meril, ki jih lahko "
"projekti KDE/FOSS enostavno dokumentirajo in zagotovijo (kar je že večina "
"dela). Za celotna merila glejte razdelek 3.1.3 v [osnovnih merilih za "
"podelitev](https://www.blauer-engel.de/en/productworld/resources-and-energy-"
"efficient-software-products)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1064
msgid "2.1 Data Formats"
msgstr "2.1 Formati podatkov"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1066
msgid "The main information to include in documentation:"
msgstr "Glavne informacije, ki jih je treba vključiti v dokumentacijo:"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1068
msgid ""
"Which (open) data formats are supported&mdash;with links to specifications, "
"e.g., [PDF](https://www.iso.org/standard/51502.html)?"
msgstr ""
"Katere (odprte) oblike podatkov so podprte – s povezavami do specifikacij, "
"npr. [PDF](https://www.iso.org/standard/51502.html)?"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1070
msgid ""
"Also of interest: Are there examples of other software products that process "
"these data formats?"
msgstr ""
"Zanimivo tudi: Ali obstajajo primeri drugih programskih izdelkov, ki "
"obdelujejo te oblike podatkov?"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1072
msgid ""
"For an example of the online documentation of supported data formats for "
"Okular, visit [the Okular website](https://okular.kde.org/formats/)."
msgstr ""
"Za primer spletne dokumentacije podprtih oblik podatkov za Okular obiščite "
"[spletno mesto Okular](https://okular.kde.org/formats/)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1074
msgid ""
"An example of documentation for the Blue Angel can be found in [Annex 4]"
"(https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/blue-angel-application/-/blob/master/"
"applications/okular/de-uz-215-eng-annex-4-okular.md)."
msgstr ""
"Primer dokumentacije za Blue Angel najdete v [Prilogi 4](https://invent.kde."
"org/teams/eco/blue-angel-application/-/blob/master/applications/okular/de-"
"uz-215-eng-annex-4-okular.md)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1077
msgid "2.2 Transparency Of The Software Product"
msgstr "2.2 Preglednost programskega izdelka"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1079
msgid ""
"When missing, provide links to documentation of the API, source code, and "
"software license. For example, for KMail:"
msgstr ""
"Če manjkajo, navedite povezave do dokumentacije API-ja, izvorne kode in "
"licence za programsko opremo. Na primer, za KMail:"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1081
msgid "[KDE PIM API documentation](https://api.kde.org/kdepim/index.html)"
msgstr "[Dokumentacija za KDE PIM API](https://api.kde.org/kdepim/index.html)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1083
msgid "[Source code](https://invent.kde.org/pim/kmail)"
msgstr "[Izvorna koda](https://invent.kde.org/pim/kmail)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1085
msgid "[License](https://invent.kde.org/pim/kmail/-/blob/master/LICENSES)"
msgstr "[Licenca](https://invent.kde.org/pim/kmail/-/blob/master/LICENSES)"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1087
msgid ""
"An example of documentation for the Blue Angel can be found in [Annex 5]"
"(https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/blue-angel-application/-/blob/master/"
"applications/kmail/de-uz-215-eng-annex-5-kmail.md)."
msgstr ""
"Primer dokumentacije za Blue Angel najdete v [Prilogi 5](https://invent.kde."
"org/teams/eco/blue-angel-application/-/blob/master/applications/kmail/de-"
"uz-215-eng-annex-5-kmail.md)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1090
msgid "2.3 Continuity Of Support"
msgstr "2.3 Neprekinjenost podpore"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1092
msgid "Details about continuity of support to document include:"
msgstr "Podrobnosti o neprekinjenosti podpore za dokument vključujejo:"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1094
msgid ""
"Information about how long the software has been supported for (with links "
"to release announcements)."
msgstr ""
"Informacije o tem, kako dolgo je programska oprema podprta (s povezavami do "
"obvestil o izdajah)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1096
msgid "Release schedule and details (e.g., who maintains the software)."
msgstr "Razpored in podrobnosti izdaj (npr. kdo vzdržuje programsko opremo)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1098
msgid "Statement that updates are free of charge."
msgstr "Izjavo, da so posodobitve brezplačne."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1100
msgid ""
"Declaration on how the free and open source software license enables "
"continuous support indefinitely."
msgstr ""
"Izjava o tem, kako licenca za prosto in odprtokodno programsko opremo "
"omogoča neprekinjeno podporo za nedoločen čas."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1102
msgid ""
"Information about whether and how functional and security updates may be "
"installed separately."
msgstr ""
"Informacije o tem, ali in kako je mogoče funkcionalne in varnostne "
"posodobitve namestiti ločeno."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1104
msgid ""
"An example of Okular’s continuity of support documentation for the Blue "
"Angel can be found in Section 3.1.3.3 of [Annex 6](https://invent.kde.org/"
"teams/eco/blue-angel-application/-/blob/master/applications/okular/de-uz-215-"
"eng-annex-6-okular.md)."
msgstr ""
"Primer dokumentacije o neprekinjenosti podpore za Okular za Blue Angel "
"najdete v razdelku 3.1.3.3 [Priloge 6] (https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/"
"blue-angel-application/-/blob/master/applications/okular/de-uz-215-eng-"
"annex-6-okular.md)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1106
msgid "2.4 Uninstallability"
msgstr "2.4 Odstranljivost"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1108
msgid ""
"How are users able to completely uninstall the software? Relevant details "
"might include:"
msgstr ""
"Kako lahko uporabniki popolnoma odstranijo programsko opremo? Ustrezne "
"podrobnosti lahko vključujejo:"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1110
msgid ""
"Uninstallation instructions that depend on how the software was installed "
"(source code or binary)."
msgstr ""
"Navodila za odstranitev, ki so odvisna od načina namestitve programske "
"opreme (izvorna koda ali binarna datoteka)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1112
msgid ""
"Examples of uninstallation instructions (source code or package managers, "
"with relevant links to documentation)."
msgstr ""
"Primere navodil za odstranitev (izvorna koda ali upravitelji paketov z "
"ustreznimi povezavami do dokumentacije)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1114
msgid ""
"Information about whether user-generated data is also removed when "
"uninstalling a program."
msgstr ""
"Informacije o tem, ali se pri odstranitvi programa odstranijo tudi podatki, "
"ki jih ustvari uporabnik."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1116
msgid ""
"An example of Okular’s uninstallability documentation for the Blue Angel can "
"be found in Section 3.1.3.4 of [Annex 6](https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/"
"blue-angel-application/-/blob/master/applications/okular/de-uz-215-eng-"
"annex-6-okular.md)."
msgstr ""
"Primer dokumentacije o možnosti odstranitve programa Blue Angel v Okularju "
"najdete v razdelku 3.1.3.4 [Priloge 6](https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/blue-"
"angel-application/-/blob/master/applications/okular/de-uz-215-eng-annex-6-"
"okular.md)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1118
msgid "2.5 Offline Capability"
msgstr "2.5 Zmogljivost brez povezave"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1120
msgid ""
"Does the software require external connections such as a license server in "
"order to run? If not, and no network connection is needed as the software "
"can be used offline, this should be documented."
msgstr ""
"Ali programska oprema za delovanje potrebuje zunanje povezave, kot je "
"licenčni strežnik? Če ne in ni potrebna omrežna povezava, saj se programska "
"oprema lahko uporablja brez povezave, je treba to dokumentirati."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1122
msgid ""
"An example of Okular’s offline capability documentation for the Blue Angel "
"can be found in Section 3.1.3.5 of [Annex 6](https://invent.kde.org/teams/"
"eco/blue-angel-application/-/blob/master/applications/okular/de-uz-215-eng-"
"annex-6-okular.md)."
msgstr ""
"Primer dokumentacije o zmogljivostih brez povezave v Okularju za Blue Angel "
"najdete v razdelku 3.1.3.5 [Priloge 6] (https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/"
"blue-angel-application/-/blob/master/applications/okular/de-uz-215-eng-"
"annex-6-okular.md)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1124
msgid "2.6 Modularity"
msgstr "2.6 Modularnost"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1126
msgid "Information to document includes:"
msgstr "Informacije, ki jih je treba dokumentirati, vključujejo:"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1128
msgid ""
"What aspects of the software are modular and can be deactivated during "
"installation?"
msgstr ""
"Kateri vidiki programske opreme so modularni in jih je mogoče med "
"namestitvijo deaktivirati?"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1130
msgid "Can the software manuals or translations be installed separately?"
msgstr ""
"Ali je mogoče priročnike ali prevode programske opreme namestiti ločeno?"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1132
msgid ""
"Are any modules which are unrelated to the core functionality included with "
"installation, such as tracking modules or cloud integration? If not, "
"document it!"
msgstr ""
"Ali so v namestitev vključeni kakšni moduli, ki niso povezani z osnovno "
"funkcionalnostjo, kot so moduli za sledenje ali integracija z oblakom? Če "
"niso, jih dokumentirajte!"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1134
msgid ""
"An example of Okular’s modularity documentation for the Blue Angel can be "
"found in Section 3.1.3.6 of [Annex 6](https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/blue-"
"angel-application/-/blob/master/applications/okular/de-uz-215-eng-annex-6-"
"okular.md)."
msgstr ""
"Primer dokumentacije o modularnosti Okularja za Blue Angel najdete v "
"razdelku 3.1.3.6 [Priloge 6] (https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/blue-angel-"
"application/-/blob/master/applications/okular/de-uz-215-eng-annex-6-okular."
"md)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1136
msgid "2.7 Freedom From Advertising"
msgstr "2.7 Brez oglaševanja"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1138
msgid ""
"If the software does not display advertising, make this explicit in manuals "
"and wikis and declare it in the Blue Angel application document."
msgstr ""
"Če programska oprema ne prikazuje oglasov, to izrecno navedite v priročnikih "
"in wikijih ter deklarirajte v dokumentu aplikacije Blue Angel."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1140
msgid "2.8 Documentation"
msgstr "2.8 Dokumentacija"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1142
msgid "This includes the following:"
msgstr "To vključuje naslednje:"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1144
msgid ""
"General process for installing/uninstalling the software? This may include "
"generic instructions or tutorials for a specific desktop environment or "
"package manager."
msgstr ""
"Splošni postopek namestitve/odstranitve programske opreme? To lahko "
"vključuje splošna navodila ali vadnice za določeno namizno okolje ali "
"upravitelja paketov."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1146
msgid "Data import/export process?"
msgstr "Postopek uvoza/izvoza podatkov?"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1148
msgid ""
"What can users do to reduce the use of resources (e.g., configuration "
"options for improving performance)?"
msgstr ""
"Kaj lahko uporabniki storijo za zmanjšanje porabe virov (npr. možnosti "
"konfiguracije za izboljšanje delovanja)?"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1150
msgid ""
"Does the software have any resource-intensive functionality not necessary "
"for the core functionality? If not, great. Let’s tell the users!"
msgstr ""
"Ali ima programska oprema kakšno funkcionalnost, ki zahteva veliko virov in "
"ni potrebna za osnovno funkcionalnost? Če ne, odlično. Povejte uporabnikom!"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1152
msgid ""
"Licensing terms related to further development of the software products, "
"with links to source code and license?"
msgstr ""
"Licenčni pogoji, povezani z nadaljnjim razvojem programskih izdelkov, s "
"povezavami do izvorne kode in licence?"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1154
msgid "Who supports the development of the software?"
msgstr "Kdo podpira razvoj programske opreme?"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1156
msgid ""
"Does the software collect any personal data? Is is compliant with existing "
"data protection laws? If yes, document it!"
msgstr ""
"Ali programska oprema zbira kakršne koli osebne podatke? Ali je skladna z "
"obstoječimi zakoni o varstvu podatkov? Če je odgovor pritrdilen, to "
"dokumentirajte!"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1158
msgid ""
"What is the privacy policy? Is there telemetry? If yes, how does the "
"software handle data security, data collection, and data transmission? Also, "
"are there ads or tracking embedded in the software? If not, excellent&mdash;"
"now make sure to spread the word!"
msgstr ""
"Kakšna je politika zasebnosti? Ali obstaja telemetrija? Če je odgovor "
"pritrdilen, kako programska oprema obravnava varnost podatkov, zbiranje "
"podatkov in prenos podatkov? Ali so v programsko opremo vgrajeni oglasi ali "
"sledenje? Če ne, odlično – zdaj poskrbite, da boste to razširili!"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1160
msgid ""
"An example of Okular’s product documentation for Blue Angel certification "
"can be found in Section 3.1.3.8 of [Annex 6](https://invent.kde.org/teams/"
"eco/blue-angel-application/-/blob/master/applications/okular/de-uz-215-eng-"
"annex-6-okular.md)."
msgstr ""
"Primer dokumentacije izdelka Okular za certifikat Blue Angel najdete v "
"razdelku 3.1.3.8 [Priloge 6] (https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/blue-angel-"
"application/-/blob/master/applications/okular/de-uz-215-eng-annex-6-okular."
"md)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1162
msgid "Submitting To RAL"
msgstr "Oddaja RALu"

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1164
msgid ""
"For examples of all of the above documentation, see KDE’s [Blue Angel "
"Applications](https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/blue-angel-application) "
"repository."
msgstr ""
"Za primere vse zgoraj navedene dokumentacije glejte repozitorij KDE [Blue "
"Angel Applications](https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/blue-angel-application)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1166
msgid ""
"Once you have all of the documentation prepared, you need to submit it for "
"review to RAL gGmbH (if you recall, RAL is the authorized body that assesses "
"compliance with the award criteria). The portal for submitting Blue Angel "
"applications can be found [here](https://portal.ral-umwelt.de/) (https://"
"portal.ral-umwelt.de/)."
msgstr ""
"Ko imate vso dokumentacijo pripravljeno, jo morate predložiti v pregled RAL "
"gGmbH (če se spomnite, je RAL pooblaščeni organ, ki ocenjuje skladnost z "
"merili za dodelitev). Portal za oddajo vlog Blue Angel najdete [tukaj]"
"(https://portal.ral-umwelt.de/) (https://portal.ral-umwelt.de/)."

#: content/be4foss-handbook/handbook_web.md:1168
msgid ""
"If you need help with the online interface, RAL provides [documentation]"
