#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:0
msgid "Opt Green: KDE Eco's New Sustainable Software Project"
msgstr "Opt Green: Novi projekt trajnostne programske opreme KDE Eco"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:0
msgid "Sustainable Software"
msgstr "Trajnostna programska oprema"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:0
msgid "Sustainable Hardware"
msgstr "Trajnostna strojna oprema"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:0
msgid ""
"KDE Eco has begun a new initiative \"Opt Green: Sustainable Software For "
"Sustainable Hardware\"."
msgstr ""
"KDE Eco je začel novo pobudo \"Opt Green: Trajnostna programska oprema za "
"trajnostno strojno opremo\"."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:0
#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:0
msgid "/blog/thumbnails/blog-opt-green-optimized.png"
msgstr "/blog/thumbnails/blog-opt-green-optimized.png"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:14
msgid ""
"Inspired by the successes of the [\"Blauer Engel Für FOSS\" (BE4FOSS)]"
"(https://eco.kde.org/blog/2022-01-25-resource-efficient-software-and-blauer-"
"engel-eco-certification/) project and KDE's ongoing [Sustainable Software]"
"(https://community.kde.org/Goals/Sustainable_Software) goal, KDE Eco has "
"begun a new initiative: \"[Opt Green](https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/opt-"
"green): Sustainable Software For Sustainable Hardware\" (German: "
"[*Nachhaltige Software Für Nachhaltige Hardware*](https://www."
"umweltbundesamt.de/das-uba/was-wir-tun/foerdern-beraten/verbaendefoerderung/"
"projektfoerderungen-projekttraeger/opt-green-nachhaltige-software-fuer-"
"nachhaltige))."
msgstr ""
"Navdihnjen z uspehi [\"Blauer Engel Für FOSS\" (BE4FOSS)](https://eco.kde."
"org/blog/2022-01-25-resource-efficient-software-and-blauer-engel-eco-"
"certification/) in stalnim ciljem KDE [Trajnostna programska oprema](https://"
"community.kde.org/Goals/Sustainable_Software), je KDE Eco začel novo pobudo: "
"\"[Opt Green](https://invent.kde. org/teams/eco/opt-green): Trajnostna "
"programska oprema za trajnostno strojno opremo\" (nemško: [*Nachhaltige "
"Software Für Nachhaltige Hardware*](https://www.umweltbundesamt.de/das-uba/"
"was-wir-tun/foerdern-beraten/verbaendefoerderung/projektfoerderungen-"
"projekttraeger/opt-green-nachhaltige-software-fuer-nachhaltige))."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:16
msgid "Opt Green: Sustainable Software For Sustainable Hardware"
msgstr "Opt Green: Trajnostna programska oprema za trajnostno strojno opremo"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:18
msgid ""
"By design, Free Software guarantees [transparency and user autonomy](https://"
"fsfe.org/freesoftware/index.en.html). This gives *you*, the user, control of "
"*your* hardware by removing unnecessary vendor dependencies. With Free "
"Software, you're able to use your devices how you want, for as long as you "
"want. There's no [bloatware](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_bloat) "
"and you can block [unwanted data use and ads](https://groenlinks.nl/sites/"
"groenlinks/files/2021-09/CE_Delft_210166_Carbon_footprint_unwanted_data-"
"use_smartphones.pdf) from driving up energy demands and slowing down your "
"device&mdash;while shutting the door to uninvited snooping in your private "
"life as well. With software made for your needs and not the vendors', you "
"can choose applications designed for the hardware you already own. Say "
"goodbye to premature hardware obsolescence: lean, efficient Free Software "
"runs on devices which are decades old!"
msgstr ""
"Zasnova proste programske opreme zagotavlja [transparentnost in avtonomijo "
"uporabnika](https://fsfe.org/freesoftware/index.en.html). To daje *vam*, "
"uporabnikom, nadzor nad *vašo* strojno opremo z odstranitvijo nepotrebnih "
"odvisnosti od prodajalca. S prosto programsko opremo lahko svoje naprave "
"uporabljate tako, kot želite, tako dolgo, kot želite. Ni [bloatware](https://"
"en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_bloat) in lahko blokirate [neželeno uporabo "
"podatkov in oglase](https://groenlinks.nl/sites/groenlinks/files/2021-09/"
"CE_Delft_210166_Carbon_footprint_unwanted_data-use_smartphones.pdf) zaradi "
"povečanja potreb po energiji in upočasnjevanja vaše naprave&mdash;pri tem pa "
"zaprete vrata tudi nepovabljenemu vohljanju glede vašega zasebnega "
"življenja. S programsko opremo, izdelano za vaše potrebe in ne za potrebe "
"prodajalcev, lahko izberete aplikacije, zasnovane za strojno opremo, ki jo "
"že imate. Poslovite se od prezgodnje zastarelosti strojne opreme: vitka, "
"učinkovita prosta programska oprema deluje na napravah, ki so stare "
"desetletja!"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:20
msgid ""
"Independent and sustainable Free Software is good for the users, and good "
"for the environment."
msgstr ""
"Neodvisna in trajnostna prosta programska oprema je dobra za uporabnike in "
"dobra za okolje."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:24
msgid ""
"![The [\"Think Global, Act Local\" campaign](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Think_globally,_act_locally) urged people to consider global health while "
"taking action in their local communities. This new project urges people to "
"do the same, but with computing. (Image from Karanjot Singh published under "
"a [CC-BY-4.0](https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html) license.)](/blog/"
"images/2024-05-24_ThinkGlobalComputeLocal.png)"
msgstr ""
"![Kampanja [\"Misli globalno, deluj lokalno - Think Global, Act Local\"]"
"(https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Think_globally,_act_locally) je ljudi "
"pozvala, naj med ukrepanjem v svojih lokalnih skupnostih upoštevajo globalno "
"zdravje. Ta novi projekt poziva ljudi, naj storijo enako, vendar z "
"računalništvom. (Slika Karanjota Singha, objavljena pod licenco [CC-BY-4.0]"
"(https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html) license.)](/blog/"
"images/2024-05-24_ThinkGlobalComputeLocal.png)"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:28
msgid ""
"Over the next two years, the \"Opt Green\" initiative will bring what KDE "
"Eco has been doing for sustainable software directly to end users. A "
"particular target group for the project is those whose consumer behavior is "
"driven by principles related to the environment, and not just price or "
"convenience: the \"eco-consumers\"."
msgstr ""
"V naslednjih dveh letih bo pobuda \"Opt Green\" to, kar KDE Eco počne za "
"trajnostno programsko opremo, prinesla to neposredno končnim uporabnikom. "
"Posebna ciljna skupina projekta so tisti, katerih vedenje potrošnikov "
"temelji na načelih, povezanih z okoljem, in ne le na ceni ali udobjem: \"eko-"
"potrošniki\"."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:30
msgid ""
"Through online and offline campaigns as well as installation workshops, we "
"will demonstrate the power of Free Software to drive down resource and "
"energy consumption, and keep devices in use for the lifespan of the "
"hardware, not the software."
msgstr ""
"S spletnimi in nespletnimi kampanjami ter namestitvenimi delavnicami bomo "
"prikazali moč proste programske opreme za zmanjšanje porabe virov in "
"energije ter ohranjanje naprav v uporabi za celotno življenjsko dobo strojne "
"opreme, ne programske opreme."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:32
msgid ""
"Our motto: **The most environmentally-friendly device is the one you already "
"own.**"
msgstr ""
"Naš moto: **Najbolj okolju prijazna naprava je tista, ki jo že imate.**"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:34
msgid ""
"The topic of software-driven sustainability is relevant for all Free "
"Software applications and developers. We'd love to have you join us and "
"become partners in combatting the issue of software-driven environmental "
"harm. Check out the project's [Invent repository](https://invent.kde.org/"
"teams/eco/opt-green) or the [contact page](https://eco.kde.org/get-"
"involved/) to get involved today!"
msgstr ""
"Tema trajnosti, ki jo poganja programska oprema, je pomembna za vse "
"aplikacije in razvijalce proste programske opreme. Veseli bomo, če se nam "
"pridružite in postanete partnerji v boju proti okoljski škodi, ki jo "
"povzroča programska oprema. Oglejte si [repozitorij Invent](https://invent."
"kde.org/teams/eco/opt-green) ali [stran stikov](https://eco.kde.org/get-"
"involved/) projekta, da sodelujete že danes!"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:36
msgid "Software's Environmental Harm"
msgstr "Okoljska škoda programske opreme"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:38
msgid ""
"On [14 October 2025](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/lifecycle/faq/"
"windows), the end of support for Windows 10 is [estimated](https://www."
"canalys.com/insights/end-of-windows-10-support-could-turn-240-million-pcs-"
"into-e-waste) to make e-waste out of [240 million computers](https://www."
"reuters.com/technology/microsoft-ending-support-windows-10-could-send-240-"
"mln-pcs-landfills-report-2023-12-21/) ineligible for the upgrade to Windows "
"11. Moreover, macOS support for Intel-based Apple computers&mdash;the last "
"of which were sold in 2020&mdash;is [predicted](https://arstechnica.com/"
"gadgets/2023/07/with-macos-sonoma-intel-macs-are-still-getting-fewer-updates-"
"than-they-used-to/) to end (at the earliest) one year later in 2026, "
"rendering even more millions upon millions of functioning devices obsolete. "
"When users have no control over the software they rely on, they are left at "
"a security risk when software support ends ... unless, of course, they "
"purchase a new computer. (By comparison, consider that only in 2022 did "
"Linus Torvalds first [suggest ending Linux kernel support](https://www."
"phoronix.com/news/Intel-i486-Linux-Possible-Drop) for Intel 486 processors "
"from 1989. That's 33 years of support!)"
msgstr ""
"Dne [14. oktobra 2025](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/lifecycle/faq/"
"windows) je konec podpore za Windows 10 [bi ocenjeno](https://www.canalys."
"com/insights/end-of-windows-10-support-could-turn-240-million-pcs-into-e-"
"waste), naredili e-odpadke iz [240 milijonov računalnikov](https://www."
"reuters.com/technology/microsoft-ending-support-windows-10-could-send-240-"
"mln-pcs-landfills-report-2023-12-21/) neprimerne za nadgradnjo na Windows "
"11. Poleg tega se podpora macOS za sisteme Intel računalnikov Apple&mdash;"
"zadnji so bili prodani leta 2020&mdash; [predvideno](https://arstechnica.com/"
"gadgets/2023/07/with-macos-sonoma-intel-macs-are-still-getting-fewer-updates-"
"than-they-used-to/), da se konča (najprej) eno leto pozneje leta 2026, "
"zaradi česar bo še več milijonov in milijonov delujočih naprav zastarelih. "
"Ko uporabniki nimajo nadzora nad programsko opremo, na katero se zanašajo, "
"so ob prenehanju podpore za programsko opremo izpostavljeni varnostnemu "
"tveganju ... razen če seveda kupijo nov računalnik. (Za primerjavo "
"upoštevajte, da je šele leta 2022 Linus Torvalds prvi [predlagal ukinitev "
"podpore za jedro Linux](https://www.phoronix.com/news/Intel-i486-Linux-"
"Possible-Drop) za procesorje Intel 486 iz leta 1989. To je 33 let podpore!)"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:40
msgid ""
"Vendors frequently require buying a new device to support software updates. "
"All too often, this is driven by economic imperatives rather than "
"technological requirements. Moreover, while new hardware has become more and "
"more powerful, new software offering [similar or identical functionality]"
"(https://www.umweltbundesamt.de/publikationen/entwicklung-anwendung-von-"
"bewertungsgrundlagen-fuer) has frequently become less efficient and more "
"energy-intensive, which has rendered older, less powerful devices useless."
msgstr ""
"Prodajalci pogosto zahtevajo nakup nove naprave za podporo posodobitev "
"programske opreme. Vse prepogosto je to posledica gospodarskih imperativov "
"in ne tehnoloških zahtev. Poleg tega, medtem ko je nova strojna oprema "
"postajala vse močnejša, je nova programska oprema, ki ponuja [podobno ali "
"enako funkcionalnost](https://www.umweltbundesamt.de/publikationen/"
"entwicklung-anwendung-von-bewertungsgrundlagen-fuer), pogosto postala manj "
"učinkovita in bolj energetsko intenzivna, zaradi česar so starejše, manj "
"zmogljive naprave neuporabne."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:42
msgid ""
"Already in 2015 Achim Steiner, former Executive Director of the UN "
"Environment Programme (UNEP), [warned](https://news.un.org/en/"
"story/2015/05/497772) of the \"tsunami of electronic waste rolling out over "
"the world\"."
msgstr ""
"Že leta 2015 je Achim Steiner, nekdanji izvršni direktor Programa ZN za "
"okolje (UNEP), [opozoril](https://news.un.org/en/story/2015/05/497772) na "
"\"tsunami kotaljenja elektronskih odpadkov po svetu\"."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:44
msgid ""
"In 2016, 44.7 million tonnes of e-waste were generated, estimated to be "
"equivalent to 4500 Eiffel Towers. If you were to stack those Eiffel Towers "
"on top of each other, the result would be 17 times higher than Mount Everest."
msgstr ""
"Leta 2016 je bilo ustvarjenih 44,7 milijona ton e-odpadkov, kar je ocenjeno "
"na 4500 Eifflovih stolpov. Če bi te Eifflove stolpe zložili enega na "
"drugega, bi bil rezultat 17-krat višji od Mount Everesta."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:46
msgid ""
"By 2017, [United Nations University](https://web.archive.org/"
"web/20220901055133/https://unu.edu/media-relations/releases/ewaste-rises-8-"
"percent-by-weight-in-2-years.html) determined e-waste to be the [fastest "
"growing waste stream](https://www.weforum.org/reports/a-new-circular-vision-"
"for-electronics-time-for-a-global-reboot/) in the world."
msgstr ""
"Do leta 2017 je [Univerza Združenih narodov](https://web.archive.org/"
"web/20220901055133/https://unu.edu/media-relations/releases/ewaste-rises-8-"
"percent-by-weight-in-2-years.html) ugotovila, da so e-odpadki [najhitreje "
"rastoči tok odpadkov](https://www.weforum.org/reports/a-new-circular-vision-"
"for-electronics-time-for-a-global-reboot/) na svetu."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:48
msgid ""
"In 2022, the amount of e-waste reached 59.4 million tonnes, a 33% increase "
"since 2016."
msgstr ""
"Leta 2022 je količina e-odpadkov dosegla 59,4 milijona ton, kar je 33-"
"odstotno povečanje od leta 2016."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:50
msgid "The flow of e-waste continues to rise today."
msgstr "Tok e-odpadkov danes še narašča."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:54
msgid ""
"![In 2016, 44.7 million metric tons of e-waste was generated. This is "
"estimated to be equivalent to 4,500 Eiffel Towers, which, when stacked, is "
"17 times higher than Mount Everest. (Image from KDE published under a [CC-BY-"
"SA-4.0](https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-SA-4.0.html) license. Design by "
"Anita Sengupta.)](/blog/images/mountain.png)"
msgstr ""
"![Leta 2016 je nastalo 44,7 milijona metričnih ton e-odpadkov. Ocenjuje se, "
"da je to enakovredno 4.500 Eifflovim stolpom, kar je, če so zloženi, 17-krat "
"višje od Mount Everesta. (Slika iz KDE, objavljena pod licenco [CC-BY-SA-4.0]"
"(https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-SA-4.0.html). Oblikovala Anita Sengupta.)](/"
"blog/images/mountain.png)"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:58
msgid ""
"Software is a frequently unacknowledged yet significant factor for "
"sustainability. Software determines a hardware's energy consumption and "
"minimum system requirements. It determines how long a device can remain "
"safely in use. With software running on [everyday devices](https://www."
"schneier.com/blog/archives/2018/10/security_in_a_w.html), from [coffee "
"machines](https://arstechnica.com/gadgets/2014/03/keurigs-next-generation-of-"
"coffee-machines-will-have-drm-lockdown/) to smartphones, from [trains]"
"(https://arstechnica.com/tech-policy/2023/12/manufacturer-deliberately-"
"bricked-trains-repaired-by-competitors-hackers-find/) to [drones](https://"
"yewtu.be/watch?v=Nxem6yTRC4M), the role of software in keeping functioning "
"hardware in use and out of the landfill grows more critical every day."
msgstr ""
"Programska oprema je pogosto nepriznan, a pomemben dejavnik trajnosti. "
"Programska oprema določa porabo energije strojne opreme in minimalne "
"sistemske zahteve. Določa, kako dolgo lahko naprava ostane varno v uporabi. "
"S programsko opremo, ki deluje na [vsakodnevnih napravah](https://www."
"schneier.com/blog/archives/2018/10/security_in_a_w.html), od [kavnih "
"avtomatov](https://www.schneier.com/blog/archives/2018/10/security_in_a_w."
"html) do pametnih telefonov, od [vlakov](https://arstechnica.com/tech-"
"policy/2023/12/manufacturer-deliberately-bricked-trains-repaired-by-"
"competitors-hackers-find/) do [dronov](https://yewtu.be/watch?"
"v=Nxem6yTRC4M), vloga programske opreme pri ohranjanju delujoče strojne "
"opreme v uporabi in zunaj odlagališč postajajo vsak dan bolj kritična."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:60
msgid ""
"For consumers, the environmental harm may be out-of-sight and out-of-mind. "
"Yet the environment is registering its effects, from the CO2 pumped into the "
"atmosphere to the landfills that receive our discarded devices at their end "
"of life, and the air, soil, and waters around them&mdash;not to mention the "
"people and animals."
msgstr ""
"Potrošniki lahko okoljske škode ne vidijo in ne mislijo nanjo. Kljub temu "
"okolje beleži njihove učinke, od CO2, ki se črpa v ozračje, do odlagališč, "
"ki sprejemajo naše zavržene naprave ob koncu njihove življenjske dobe, ter "
"zraka, prsti in vode okoli njih - da ne omenjamo ljudi in živali."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:64
msgid ""
"![A young man is pictured burning electrical wires to recover copper at "
"Agbogbloshie, Ghana, as another metal scrap worker arrives with more wires "
"to be burned. A 2018 article in the \"International Journal of Cancer\" "
"reports a [correlation](https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1002/"
"ijc.31902) between proximity to e-waste burn sites and childhood lymphoma. "
"([Image](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Agbogbloshie,_Ghana_-"
"_September_2019.jpg) by Muntaka Chasant, published under a [CC-BY-SA-4.0]"
"(https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-SA-4.0.html) license.)](/blog/images/"
"sec1_800px-Agbogbloshie_Ghana_September_2019.webp)"
msgstr ""
"![Na sliki je mladenič, ki sežiga električne žice za pridobivanje bakra v "
"Agbogbloshieju v Gani, medtem ko pride še en delavec za kovinske odpadke z "
"več žicami, ki jih je treba požgati. Članek iz leta 2018 article v "
"\"International Journal of Cancer\" poroča o [korelaciji](https://"
"onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/abs/10.1002/ijc.31902) med bližino kurišč e-"
"odpadkov in limfomov pri otrocih. ([Image](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"File:Agbogbloshie,_Ghana_-_September_2019.jpg) avtorja Munthaka Chasant, "
"objavljeno pod [CC-BY-SA-4.0](https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-SA-4.0.html) "
"license.)](/blog/images/sec1_800px-Agbogbloshie_Ghana_September_2019.webp)"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:68
msgid ""
"It is particularly devastating when you consider the environmental and "
"social harm caused by e-waste, especially when e-waste is generated earlier "
"than necessary because of premature obsolescence. The production and "
"transportation of a device accounts for 50&ndash;80+% of its carbon "
"footprint over its lifecycle. A [German Environment Report](http://www.uba."
"de/uba-info-medien/4316.html) estimates you’d need to use a computer for "
"over 30 years before efficiency gains in newly-produced devices justify "
"their purchase."
msgstr ""
"To je še posebej uničujoče, če pomislite na okoljsko in družbeno škodo, ki "
"jo povzročajo e-odpadki, še posebej, če e-odpadki nastanejo prej, kot je "
"potrebno, zaradi prezgodnje zastarelosti. Proizvodnja in transport naprave "
"predstavljata 50&ndash;80+ % njenega ogljičnega odtisa v njenem življenjskem "
"ciklu. [Nemško okoljsko poročilo](http://www.uba.de/uba-info-medien/4316."
"html) ocenjuje, da bi morali računalnik uporabljati več kot 30 let, preden "
"bi povečanje učinkovitosti na novo proizvedenih naprav upravičilo nakup."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:70
msgid ""
"Furthermore, the extraction of rare earth metals in production consumes "
"copious amounts of energy and takes place under miserable social conditions, "
"often in the Global South. For disposal, devices are typically returned to "
"the Global South for end-of-life treatment, where they pollute the "
"environment as toxic waste and cause enormous damage to workers' health or "
"even death."
msgstr ""
"Poleg tega pridobivanje redkih zemeljskih kovin v proizvodnji porablja obilo "
"energije in poteka v bednih družbenih razmerah, pogosto na globalnem jugu. "
"Za odlaganje se naprave običajno vrnejo na globalni jug za obdelavo ob koncu "
"življenjske dobe, kjer onesnažujejo okolje kot strupeni odpadki in "
"povzročajo ogromno škodo zdravju delavcev ali celo smrt."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:74
msgid ""
"![Apple's carbon footprint. From Apple (2019), \"Environmental "
"Responsibility Report: 2019 Progress Report, covering fiscal year 2018\". "
"(Image from KDE published under a [CC-BY-SA-4.0](https://spdx.org/licenses/"
"CC-BY-SA-4.0.html) license. Design by Anita Sengupta.)](/blog/images/apple-"
"report.png)"
msgstr ""
"![Applov ogljični odtis. Od Apple (2019), \"Poročilo o okoljski "
"odgovornosti: poročilo o napredku za leto 2019, ki zajema proračunsko leto "
"2018 - Environmental Responsibility Report: 2019 Progress Report, covering "
"fiscal year 2018\". (Slika iz KDE, objavljena pod licenco [CC-BY-SA-4.0]"
"(https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-SA-4.0.html). Oblikovala Anita Sengupta.)](/"
"blog/images/apple-report.png)"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:78
msgid "Giving Consumers What They Want"
msgstr "Dati potrošnikom, kar hočejo"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:80
msgid ""
"Globally, interest in environmental harm and sustainable goods has been "
"[rising steadily from 2015 to 2021](https://www.worldwildlife.org/"
"publications/an-eco-wakening-measuring-awareness-engagement-and-action-for-"
"nature). In Europe, a [2020 Eurobarometer poll](https://europa.eu/"
"eurobarometer/surveys/detail/2228) found that 50% of consumers indicate that "
"two reasons they purchase new devices are performance issues and non-"
"functioning software, and [8 in 10 consumers](https://europa.eu/"
"eurobarometer/api/deliverable/download/file?deliverableId=72255) believe "
"manufacturers should be required to make it easier to repair digital devices."
msgstr ""
"Na svetovni ravni zanimanje za okoljsko škodo in trajnostne dobrine [stalno "
"narašča od leta 2015 do 2021](https://www.worldwildlife.org/publications/an-"
"eco-wakening-measuring-awareness-engagement-and-action-for-nature). V Evropi "
"je [javna raziskava Eurobarometra 2020](https://europa.eu/eurobarometer/"
"surveys/detail/2228) pokazala, da 50 % potrošnikov navaja, da sta dva "
"razloga za nakup novih naprav težave z zmogljivostjo in nedelujoča "
"programska oprema ter [8 od 10 potrošnikov](https://europa.eu/eurobarometer/"
"api/deliverable/download/file?deliverableId=72255) meni, da je treba od "
"proizvajalcev zahtevati, da olajšajo popravilo digitalnih naprav."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:82
msgid ""
"Free Software already gives consumers what they want, but most don't know it "
"yet. Transparency in code makes lightweight, highly performative software "
"possible, even on much older devices, while user autonomy ensures the right "
"to repair when applications stop functioning."
msgstr ""
"Prosta programska oprema potrošnikom že nudi, kar si želijo, vendar se "
"večina tega še ne zaveda. Transparentnost kode omogoča enostavno in visoko "
"zmogljivo programsko opremo, tudi na veliko starejših napravah, medtem ko "
"avtonomija uporabnika zagotavlja pravico do popravila, ko aplikacije "
"prenehajo delovati."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:86
msgid ""
"![KDE’s popular multi-platform PDF reader and universal document viewer "
"Okular was awarded the Blue Angel ecolabel in 2022. (Image from KDE "
"published under a [CC-BY-4.0](https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html) "
"license.)](/blog/images/sec2_okular-BE-logo.png)"
msgstr ""
"![KDE-jev priljubljen večplatformski bralnik PDF in univerzalni "
"pregledovalnik dokumentov Okular je bil leta 2022 nagrajen z znakom za "
"okolje Blue Angel. (Slika iz KDE, objavljena pod licenco  [CC-BY-4.0]"
"(https://spdx.org/licenses/CC-BY-4.0.html)](/blog/images/sec2_okular-BE-logo."
"png)"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:90
msgid ""
"In fact, the [Blue Angel criteria for desktop software](https://www.blauer-"
"engel.de/en/productworld/resources-and-energy-efficient-software-products) "
"are at the forefront in recognizing the critical role of transparency and "
"user autonomy in sustainable software design. From 2021-2023, the KDE Eco "
"project \"Blauer Engel Für FOSS\" (BE4FOSS) had the goal of collecting and "
"spreading information about the Blue Angel ecolabel among developer "
"communities. In 2022, KDE’s popular PDF and universal document reader "
"[Okular](https://okular.kde.org/eco) became the [first ever Blue Angel eco-"
"certified software](https://eco.kde.org/blog/2022-03-16-press-release-okular-"
"blue-angel/)! The BE4FOSS project culminated with the KDE Eco handbook "
"\"Applying The Blue Angel Criteria To Free Software\", which you can read "
"[here](https://eco.kde.org/handbook/). KDE's [Sustainable Software](https://"
"community.kde.org/Goals/Sustainable_Software) goal has continued this work "
"by developing [emulation tools](https://eco.kde.org/categories/kdeecotest/) "
"like [KdeEcoTest](https://eco.kde.org/blog/2024-02-20-windows-kdeecotest-"
"support/) and [Selenium AT-SPI](https://eco.kde.org/categories/selenium/) to "
"measure software's energy consumption in KDE's [KEcoLab](https://eco.kde.org/"
"categories/kecolab/)."
msgstr ""
"Pravzaprav so [kriteriji Modrega Angela za namizno programsko opremo - Blue "
"Angel criteria for desktop software](https://www.blauer-engel.de/en/"
"productworld/resources-and-energy-efficient-software-products) v ospredju "
"pri prepoznavanju kritične vloge preglednosti in avtonomije uporabnika pri "
"trajnostnem oblikovanju programske opreme. Od leta 2021 do 2023 je bil cilj "
"projekta KDE Eco »Blauer Engel Für FOSS« (BE4FOSS) zbiranje in širjenje "
"informacij o znaku za okolje Blue Angel med skupnostmi razvijalcev. Leta "
"2022 je KDE-jev priljubljen univerzalni bralnik dokumentov [Okular](https://"
"okular.kde.org/eco) postal [prva programska oprema z ekološkim certifikatom "
"Blue Angel](https://eco.kde.org/blog/2022-03-16-press-release-okular-blue-"
"angel/)! Projekt BE4FOSS je dosegel vrhunec s priročnikom KDE Eco »Uporaba "
"meril Blue Angel za prosto programsko opremo«, ki ga lahko preberete [tukaj]"
"(https://eco.kde.org/handbook/). KDE-jev cilj [Trajnostna programska oprema]"
"(https://community.kde.org/Goals/Sustainable_Software) je nadaljeval to delo "
"z razvojem [orodij za emulacijo](https://eco.kde.org/categories/"
"kdeecotest/), kot je [KdeEcoTest](https://eco.kde.org/blog/2024-02-20-"
"windows-kdeecotest-support/) in [Selenium AT-SPI](https://eco.kde.org/"
"categories/selenium/) za merjenje porabe energije programske opreme v KDE "
"[KEcoLab](https://eco.kde.org/categories/kecolab/)."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:92
msgid ""
"Now we want to take what we have achieved and bring it directly to eco-"
"consumers."
msgstr ""
"Zdaj želimo to, kar smo dosegli, prenesti neposredno do eko-potrošnikov."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:94
msgid ""
"Through educational campaigns and workshops, the \"Opt Green\" project aims "
"to combat e-waste by keeping hardware in use with Free Software. Although "
"the problem of software-driven e-waste is relevant for an increasing number "
"of digital devices, the focus will be on desktop PCs, laptops, and, when "
"possible, smartphones and tablets. We are planning to set up info-stands at "
"fair-trade, organic, and artisanal markets as well as sustainability "
"festivals such as the [Umweltfestival](https://www.umweltfestival.de/) in "
"Berlin. We will distribute [leaflets](https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/opt-"
"green/-/blob/master/materials/leaflets/EN/kde-eco-umweltfestival-flyer-"
"EN_final.jpg) to consumers, and demo vendor-abandoned devices which are not "
"only usable, but also a joy to use thanks to the tireless work of inspiring "
"Free Software communities. Installation workshops will give users the know-"
"how to keep their devices in use for as long as they want."
msgstr ""
"Z izobraževalnimi kampanjami in delavnicami se projekt \"Opt Green\" želi "
"boriti proti e-odpadkom z ohranjanjem uporabe strojne opreme s prosto "
"programsko opremo. Čeprav je problem e-odpadkov, ki jih poganja programska "
"oprema, pomemben za vse več digitalnih naprav, bo poudarek na namiznih "
"osebnih računalnikih, prenosnih računalnikih in, kadar je to mogoče, na "
"pametnih telefonih in tablicah. Načrtujemo postavitev informacijskih stojnic "
"na trgih pravične trgovine, ekoloških in obrtniških tržnicah ter na "
"trajnostnih festivalih, kot je [Umweltfestival](https://www.umweltfestival."
"de/) v Berlinu. Potrošnikom bomo razdelili [letake](https://invent.kde.org/"
"teams/eco/opt-green/-/raw/master/materials/leaflets/kde-eco-umweltfestival-"
"flyer-EN_final.jpg), in predstavitvene naprave, ki so jih zapustili "
"prodajalci, ki niso le uporabne, ampak jih je tudi veselje uporabljati, "
"zahvaljujoč neutrudnemu delu navdihovanja skupnosti proste programske "
"opreme. Namestitvene delavnice bodo uporabnikom dale znanje, kako ohranjati "
"svoje naprave v uporabi tako dolgo kot želijo."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:96
msgid ""
"Consumers don’t need a new computer to get secure, cutting-edge software; "
"they just need the right software. Free Software already gives consumers "
"what they want today, and we will be working hard to make sure they know "
"that."
msgstr ""
"Potrošniki ne potrebujejo novega računalnika, da bi dobili varno, vrhunsko "
"programsko opremo; potrebujejo le pravo programsko opremo. Prosta programska "
"oprema že danes ponuja potrošnikom, kar si želijo, in trdo se bomo trudili "
"zagotoviti, da bodo to vedeli."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:98
msgid "Ready To Join Us?"
msgstr "Ste se nam pripravljeni pridružiti?"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:100
msgid ""
"Consumers want sustainable and repairable digital devices. We believe that "
"providing users the software to keep devices in use and out of the landfill "
"will drive demand for Free Software products and enable long-term hardware "
"use."
msgstr ""
"Potrošniki želijo trajnostne in popravljive digitalne naprave. Verjamemo, da "
"bo zagotavljanje programske opreme uporabnikom za ohranjanje naprav v "
"uporabi in izven odlagališča povečalo povpraševanje po izdelkih proste "
"programske opreme in omogočilo dolgoročno uporabo strojne opreme."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:102
msgid ""
"**Do you want to join us in this movement to combat e-waste with Free "
"Software? See our [contact info](https://eco.kde.org/get-involved/) to get "
"involved.**"
msgstr ""
"**Ali se nam želite pridružiti v tem gibanju za boj proti e-odpadkom s "
"prosto programsko opremo? Oglejte si naše [kontaktne podatke](https://eco."
"kde.org/get-involved/), če želite sodelovati.**"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:104
msgid ""
"We need volunteers like you to bring the \"Opt Green\" campaign to towns and "
"cities around the world. We need volunteers like you to design engaging "
"guides and beautiful materials for global distribution. We need volunteers "
"like you to report on the project in magazines and newspapers. Let's work "
"together to bring sustainable software to your community!"
msgstr ""
"Potrebujemo prostovoljce, kot ste vi, da bi kampanjo \"Opt Green\" "
"pripeljali v kraje in mesta po vsem svetu. Potrebujemo prostovoljce, kot ste "
"vi, da oblikujete privlačne vodnike in čudovite materiale za globalno "
"distribucijo. Potrebujemo prostovoljce, kot ste vi, da bi o projektu "
"poročali v revijah in časopisih. Sodelujmo, da v vašo skupnost prinesemo "
"trajnostno programsko opremo!"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:106
msgid ""
"Maybe you are interested in contributing to the development of [measurement "
"tools](https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/) like KdeEcoTest and Selenium AT-"
"SPI or improving KEcoLab automation? Or using such tools to measure your "
"software application's energy consumption? Let's collaborate to make energy "
"transparency a part of Free Software development today!"
msgstr ""
"Morda vas zanima prispevanje k razvoju [orodij za merjenje](https://invent."
"kde.org/teams/eco/), kot sta KdeEcoTest in Selenium AT-SPI, ali izboljšanje "
"avtomatizacije KEcoLab? Ali uporabo takih orodij za merjenje porabe energije "
"vaše programske aplikacije? Sodelujmo, da bo energetska preglednost danes "
"del razvoja proste programske opreme!"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:108
msgid ""
"Or maybe you actively contribute to a Free Software project that will keep "
"hardware in use for longer. Please be in touch! We want to promote the "
"amazing work you do directly with consumers."
msgstr ""
"Ali pa morda aktivno prispevate k projektu proste programske opreme, ki bo "
"strojno opremo uporabljal dlje. Prosimo, javite se! Želimo promovirati "
"čudovito delo, ki ga opravljate neposredno s potrošniki."

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:110
msgid ""
"Additional ideas are more than welcome. Part of the project will be figuring "
"out what works and engagement by people like you will make this project a "
"success. We would love to have you join us. Learn more: https://eco.kde.org/"
"get-involved/"
msgstr ""
"Dodatne ideje so več kot dobrodošle. Del projekta bo ugotovitev, kaj deluje, "
"in angažiranost ljudi, kot ste vi, bo ta projekt naredila uspešnega. Veseli "
"bomo, če se nam pridružite. Več o tem: https://eco.kde.org/get-involved/"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:112
msgid "*Note: This post was updated on Monday, 17 June 2024.*"
msgstr ""
"*Opomba: Ta objava je bila posodobljena v ponedeljek, 17. junija 2024.*"

#: content/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh.md:116
msgid ""
"This project is funded by the Federal Environment Agency and the Federal "
"Ministry for the Environment, Nature Conservation, Nuclear Safety and "
"Consumer Protection (BMUV<sup><a id=\"fnr.1\" class=\"footref\" href="
"\"#fn.1\">1</a></sup>). The funds are made available by resolution of the "
"German Bundestag."
msgstr ""
"Projekt BE4Foss je financirala nemška Zvezna agencija za okolje in Zvezno "
"ministrstvo za okolje, ohranjanje narave, jedrsko varnost in varstvo "
"potrošnikov (BMUV<sup><a id=\"fnr.1\" class=\"footref\" href=\"#fn.1\">1</"
"a></sup>). Sredstva so na voljo z resolucijo nemškega Bundestaga."

