msgid "Opt Green"
msgstr "Opt Green"

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:0
msgid "Opt Green Has Ended. Long Live Opt Green!"
msgstr "Opt Green se je končal. Naj živi Opt Green!"

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:0
msgid "Part I: Repair Cafés"
msgstr "1. del: Servisne kavarne"

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:0
msgid "Repair"
msgstr "Popravilo"

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:0
msgid ""
"The Opt Green project has come to an end. Two activities of the project will "
"help it live on for years to come. This is Part I."
msgstr ""
"Projekt Opt Green se je zaključil. Dve dejavnosti projekta mu bosta pomagali "
"živeti še vrsto let. To je 1. del."

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:15
msgid ""
"As May came to an end, so did KDE Eco's \"Opt Green: Sustainable Software "
"For Sustainable Hardware\" (German: *Nachhaltige Software Für Nachhaltige "
"Hardware*) project. Read the [announcement](https://eco.kde.org/"
"blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh/) from 2024 at the project's start. It has "
"been a full and exciting two years. Together with a wonderful team at KDE, "
"dozens of supportive communities, and thousands of volunteers, we really "
"achieved a whole lot. Highlights include: The project organized stands at "
"[environmental festivals](https://floss.social/@be4foss/112332015705832479), "
"[markets](https://floss.social/@be4foss/114710216026030872) and the [Long "
"Night of the Sciences](https://floss.social/@be4foss/112683207939133955). We "
"did outreach at [international conferences](https://floss.social/"
"@be4foss/115150588729184584). We hosted install parties for [adults](https://"
"floss.social/@be4foss/114748408438299075) and [children](https://floss."
"social/@be4foss/113708388646578981), as well as taught [upcycling](https://"
"floss.social/@be4foss/116697191038161548) [courses](https://floss.social/"
"@be4foss/112999467563097293) in high school. We published ads, [advertorials]"
"(https://web.archive.org/web/20260330152731/https://werde-magazin.de/stories/"
"beitrag/opt-green-eine-nachhaltigere-digitale-welt-ist-moeglich/?"
"_ppp=9ff391efeb), and [articles](https://floss.social/"
"@be4foss/116798414401293997) in Free & Open Source Software (FOSS) and eco-"
"consumer magazines, and even co-authored an [academic paper](https://floss."
"social/@be4foss/115547259601891579). We built new networks between FOSS and "
"repair communities. And we [mobilized](https://floss.social/"
"@be4foss/113713173732030500) volunteers worldwide to offer in-person Linux "
"support in a [global campaign](https://floss.social/"
"@be4foss/113424955829573330) against e-waste driven by Microsoft's software "
"policies."
msgstr ""
"Kot se je končeval maj, se je končeval tudi projekt KDE Eco \"Opt Green: "
"Trajnostna programska oprema za trajnostno strojno opremo\" (nemško: "
"*Nachhaltige Software Für Nachhaltige Hardware*). Preberite [objavo](https://"
"eco.kde.org/blog/2024-05-29_introducing-ns4nh/) iz leta 2024, ko se je "
"projekt začel. Bila sta to polni in vznemirljivi dve leti. Skupaj s čudovito "
"ekipo v KDE, številnimi podpornimi skupnostmi in tisoči prostovoljcev smo "
"resnično dosegli veliko. Med pomembnejšimi dogodki so: Projekt je "
"organiziral stojnice na [okoljskih festivalih](https://floss.social/"
"@be4foss/112332015705832479), [tržnicah](https://floss.social/"
"@be4foss/114710216026030872) in [Dolgi noči znanosti](https://floss.social/"
"@be4foss/112683207939133955). Izvajali smo ozaveščanje na [mednarodnih "
"konferencah](https://floss.social/@be4foss/115150588729184584). Priredili "
"smo zabave ob namestitvi izdelkov za [odrasle](https://floss.social/"
"@be4foss/114748408438299075) in [otroke](https://floss.social/"
"@be4foss/113708388646578981), v srednji šoli pa smo poučevali [tečaje "
"upcyclinga](https://floss.social/@be4foss/116697191038161548)(https://floss."
"social/@be4foss/112999467563097293). Objavljali smo oglase, [oglasne članke]"
"(https://web.archive.org/web/20260330152731/https://werde-magazin.de/stories/"
"beitrag/opt-green-eine-nachhaltigere-digitale-welt-ist-moeglich/?"
"_ppp=9ff391efeb) in [članke](https://floss.social/"
"@be4foss/116798414401293997) v revijah o prosti in odprtokodni programski "
"opremi (FOSS) in ekoloških revijah za potrošnike ter bili celo soavtorji "
"[akademskega članka](https://floss.social/@be4foss/115547259601891579). "
"Zgradili smo nova omrežja med FOSS in skupnostmi za popravila. In "
"[mobilizirali](https://floss.social/@be4foss/113713173732030500) "
"prostovoljce po vsem svetu, da bi ponudili osebno podporo za Linux v "
"[globalni kampanji](https://floss.social/@be4foss/113424955829573330) proti "
"e-odpadkom, ki jih spodbujajo Microsoftove politike o programski opremi."

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:17
msgid "I only wish we had another two years!"
msgstr "Želim si le, da bi imeli še dve leti!"

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:21
msgid ""
"![An ad for the [End Of 10 campaign](https://endof10.org/) in a German "
"environmental magazine. Eco-consumers are a new demographic for KDE and Free "
"& Open Source Software and one of the main target groups of the Opt Green "
"project. Since publishing this ad in early 2026, Microsoft has again "
"extended the end of support for Windows 10 until 12 October 2027. (Image "
"from KDE published under a [CC BY-SA 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/"
"licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode.en) license. Design by Anita Sengupta.)](/blog/"
"images/2026-07-22-ad-werde.png)"
msgstr ""
"![Oglas za [kampanjo Konec desetke/End Of 10](https://endof10.org/) v nemški "
"okoljski reviji. Eko-potrošniki so nova demografska skupina za KDE in prosto "
"in odprtokodno programsko opremo ter ena glavnih ciljnih skupin projekta Opt "
"Green. Od objave tega oglasa v začetku leta 2026 je Microsoft ponovno "
"podaljšal konec podpore za Windows 10 do 12. oktobra 2027. (Slika iz KDE, "
"objavljena pod licenco [CC BY-SA 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/licenses/"
"by-sa/4.0/legalcode.en). Oblikovanje: Anita Sengupta.)](/blog/"
"images/2026-07-22-ad-werde.png)"

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:25
msgid ""
"I will not attempt to write a retrospective of everything the project did. "
"Instead, I would like to focus on two aspects of the project which I believe "
"will result in the main goals of the project not only continuing, but "
"thriving well beyond the project's end. This post will be published in two "
"parts. Here, in Part I, I will present Opt Green's activities in networking "
"and collaborating with Repair Cafés. In Part II, to be published soon, I "
"will take a closer look at the End Of 10 campaign and what comes next after "
"the unexpected two-year extension of Windows 10 support."
msgstr ""
"Ne bom poskušal napisati retrospektive vsega, kar je projekt naredil. "
"Namesto tega bi se rad osredotočil na dva vidika projekta, za katera "
"verjamem, da bosta privedla do tega, da se bodo glavni cilji projekta ne le "
"nadaljevali, temveč bodo tudi uspevali še dolgo po koncu projekta. Ta objava "
"bo objavljena v dveh delih. V prvem delu bom predstavil dejavnosti Opt Green "
"na področju mreženja in sodelovanja s servisnimi kavarnami. V drugem delu, "
"ki bo kmalu objavljen, si bom podrobneje ogledal kampanjo Konec desetke/End "
"Of 10 in kaj sledi po nepričakovanem dvoletnem podaljšanju podpore za "
"Windows 10."

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:27
msgid "Networking With Repair Cafés"
msgstr "Mreženje s servisnimi kavarnami"

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:29
msgid ""
"Repair collectives provide community spaces to fix stuff. There exist many "
"groups offering workshops to make and repair things, such as [Hackerspaces, "
"Makerspaces](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Makerspace), [FabLabs](https://en."
"wikipedia.org/wiki/Fablab), and [Linux User Groups](https://en.wikipedia.org/"
"wiki/Linux_User_Groups). [Repair Cafés](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/"
"Repair_Caf%C3%A9) will be the focus here, though. Free & Open Source "
"Software, and the role it plays in keeping computers in use after vendor "
"support ends, is for the most part a new topic for these communities. "
"Moreover, Repair Cafés generally serve a different demographic than "
"Hackerspaces, Fablabs, LUGs, etc. Working with Repair Cafés provides a great "
"opportunity to reach people well outside the FOSS bubble."
msgstr ""
"Kolektivi popravljalnic zagotavljajo skupnostne prostore za popravilo "
"stvari. Obstaja veliko skupin, ki ponujajo delavnice za izdelavo in "
"popravilo stvari, kot so [Hackerspaces, Makerspaces](https://en.wikipedia."
"org/wiki/Makerspace), [FabLabs](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fablab) in "
"[Linux User Groups](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linux_User_Groups). Vendar "
"se bomo tukaj osredotočili na [Servisne kavarne - Repair Cafés](https://en."
"wikipedia.org/wiki/Repair_Caf%C3%A9). Prosta in odprtokodna programska "
"oprema ter njena vloga pri ohranjanju uporabe računalnikov po koncu podpore "
"prodajalcev je za te skupnosti večinoma nova tema. Poleg tega popravljalnice "
"kavarne običajno služijo drugačni demografski skupini kot Hackerspaces, "
"Fablabs, LUG itd. Sodelovanje s popravljalnicami kavarnami ponuja odlično "
"priložnost za doseganje ljudi daleč zunaj mehurčka FOSS."

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:31
msgid ""
"Repair Cafés are a place to repair objects used in everyday life, such as "
"clothing, electronics, bicycles, and so on. The first Repair Café was "
"launched in Holland in 2009 by Dutch journalist Martine Postma. Since then "
"thousands have popped up around the world with support from organizations "
"such as [Repair Cafe International](https://www.repaircafe.org/) (started by "
"Martine Postma), the [Restart Project](https://therestartproject.org/) "
"(creators of Right To Repair and Open Repair Alliance), [iFixit](https://www."
"ifixit.com), [anstiftung](https://anstiftung.de/), among others."
msgstr ""
"Servisne kavarne so prostor za popravilo predmetov, ki se uporabljajo v "
"vsakdanjem življenju, kot so oblačila, elektronika, kolesa in tako naprej. "
"Prvo servisno kavarno je leta 2009 na Nizozemskem odprla nizozemska "
"novinarka Martine Postma. Od takrat so se po vsem svetu pojavile tisoče s "
"podporo organizacij, kot so [Repair Cafe International](https://www."
"repaircafe.org/) (ki jo je ustanovila Martine Postma), [Restart Project]"
"(https://therestartproject.org/) (ustanovitelji organizacij Pravice do "
"popravila - Right To Repair in Open Repair Alliance), [iFixit](https://www."
"ifixit.com), [anstiftung](https://anstiftung.de/) in druge."

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:35
msgid ""
"![Screenshot from anstiftung's [Netzwerk Reparatur-Initiativen](https://www."
"reparatur-initiativen.de/) website. Those little sunny dots on the right "
"show the location of Repair Cafés around Germany.](/blog/images/2026-07-22-"
"anstiftung.png)"
msgstr ""
"![Posnetek zaslona s spletne strani fundacije anstiftung [Omrežje pobud za "
"popravila](https://www.reparatur-initiativen.de/). Tiste majhne sončne "
"pikice na desni prikazujejo lokacijo servisnih kavarn po Nemčiji.](/blog/"
"images/2026-07-22-anstiftung.png)"

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:40
msgid "From Skepticism, To Support"
msgstr "Od skepticizma do podpore"

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:42
msgid ""
"The project's outreach to Repair Cafés in Germany started at the end of 2024 "
"and early 2025. We were initially met with some skepticism. Software was "
"simply not seen as being of interest to repair communities. Hardware, yes; "
"anything related to real physical objects, sure. But software, not so much."
msgstr ""
"Projekt se je začel ukvarjati s servisnimi kavarnami v Nemčiji konec leta "
"2024 in v začetku leta 2025. Sprva smo bili deležni nekaj skepticizma. "
"Programska oprema preprosto ni bila zanimiva za skupnosti, ki se ukvarjajo s "
"popravilom. Strojna oprema, ja; vse, kar je povezano z resničnimi fizičnimi "
"predmeti, seveda. Vendar programska oprema ne preveč."

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:44
msgid ""
"One of Opt Green's goals was to raise awareness about how software is as "
"important to hardware longevity as physical components like batteries, "
"cables, and screens. The repair motto \"Repair Instead Of Throw Away\" (in "
"German: \"[*Reparieren statt Wegwerfen*](https://anstiftung.de/praxis/"
"reparieren)\") was perfectly in line with Opt Green's goals. The project had "
"even adopted mottos with similar messages: \"The most environmentally-"
"friendly device is the one you already own!\" and \"You don't need a new "
"computer&mdash;you just need the right software!\" So we kept at it."
msgstr ""
"Eden od ciljev projekta Opt Green je bil ozaveščanje o tem, kako pomembna je "
"programska oprema za dolgo življenjsko dobo strojne opreme kot fizične "
"komponente, kot so baterije, kabli in zasloni. Moto »Popravi namesto "
"zavrzi« (v nemščini: »[*Reparieren statt Wegwerfen*](https://anstiftung.de/"
"praxis/reparieren)«) je bil popolnoma v skladu s cilji projekta Opt Green. "
"Projekt je celo sprejel gesla s podobnimi sporočili: »Najbolj okolju "
"prijazna naprava je tista, ki jo že imate!« in »Ne potrebujete novega "
"računalnika – potrebujete le pravo programsko opremo!« Zato smo nadaljevali."

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:46
msgid ""
"The project's first major platform to reach the German repair community was "
"at an [online presentation in March 2025](https://web.archive.org/"
"web/20250405225518/https://www.reparatur-initiativen.de/post/das-ende-von-"
"windows10-und-wie-man-pcs-und-laptops-danach-noch-nutzen-kann) organized by "
"Opt Green with the repair organization [anstiftung](https://anstiftung.de/). "
"In the talk, we underscored how software [drives e-waste](https://www."
"reparatur-initiativen.de/files/kcfinder/posts/97597/2025-03-24-KDE-linux-"
"anstiftung.pdf) along with other forms of energy and resource consumption. "
"We showed how software repair&mdash;which FOSS licenses make possible&mdash;"
"could extend the operating life of devices to reduce the environmental harm "
"of hardware production, transportation, and disposal."
msgstr ""
"Prva večja platforma projekta, ki je dosegla nemško skupnost serviserjev, je "
"bila na [spletni predstavitvi marca 2025](https://web.archive.org/"
"web/20250405225518/https://www.reparatur-initiativen.de/post/das-ende-von-"
"windows10-und-wie-man-pcs-und-laptops-danach-noch-nutzen-kann) organizirana "
"od Opt Green z organizacijo za popravila [anstiftung](https://anstiftung."
"de/). V pogovoru smo poudarili, kako programska oprema [poganja e-odpadke]"
"(https://www.reparatur-initiativen.de/files/kcfinder/posts/97597/2025-03-24-"
"KDE-linux-anstiftung.pdf) skupaj z drugimi oblikami porabe energije in "
"virov. Pokazali smo, kako lahko popravilo programske opreme – ki ga "
"omogočajo licence FOSS – podaljša življenjsko dobo naprav in tako zmanjša "
"okoljsko škodo zaradi proizvodnje, transporta in odstranjevanja strojne "
"opreme."

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:48
msgid ""
"Around 180 Repair Café volunteers participated … and we were pleasantly "
"suprised to learn that a handful of volunteers were already offering FOSS "
"support in their Repair Cafés!"
msgstr ""
"Sodelovalo je približno 180 prostovoljcev servisnih kavarn ... in prijetno "
"presenečeni smo bili, ko smo izvedeli, da peščica prostovoljcev že ponuja "
"podporo FOSS v svojih servisnih kavarnah!"

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:50
msgid ""
"The first meetup was such a success that together with anstiftung we "
"organized a [follow-up webinar in May](https://www.reparatur-initiativen.de/"
"post/das-ende-von-windows10-und-wie-man-pcs-und-laptops-danach-noch-nutzen-"
"kann) with End Of 10 contributors Varut & Herbert. A heartfelt thank you to "
"both for presenting! What a joy to see at the second event again over 100 "
"Repair Café volunteers interested to learn how to install and use FOSS on "
"their own devices."
msgstr ""
"Prvo srečanje je bilo tako uspešno, da smo skupaj z organizacijo anstiftung "
"maja organizirali [nadaljevalni spletni seminar](https://www.reparatur-"
"initiativen.de/post/das-ende-von-windows10-und-wie-man-pcs-und-laptops-"
"danach-noch-nutzen-kann) s sodelavcema Konec desetke/End Of 10, Varutom in "
"Herbertom. Iskrena hvala obema za predstavitev! Kakšno veselje je bilo na "
"drugem dogodku spet videti več kot 100 prostovoljcev servisnih kavarn, ki "
"jih zanima, kako namestiti in uporabljati FOSS na svojih napravah."

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:52
msgid "It seems that software is indeed of interest to repair communities!"
msgstr ""
"Videti je, da je programska oprema resnično zanimiva za skupnosti, ki se "
"ukvarjajo s popravilom!"

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:54
msgid ""
"As of July 2026, a little over one year after that second webinar, on the "
"End Of 10 website there are 85+ places and 170+ events listed from Repair "
"Cafés, Linux Cafés (i.e., repair cafés focused specifically on Linux), and "
"similar organizations like IT-Cafés, Technik-Cafés, etc. (Once you include "
"the Makerspaces, Hackerspaces, Fablabs, LUGs, and other initiatives that "
"stepped up to help out, there are over 1180 places and events in total on "
"the End Of 10 website&mdash;more on that in Part II.) Moreover, Repair Café "
"International, an [End Of 10 supporting organization](https://endof10.org/"
"#supporters), now lists 40 [Linux Repair Cafés](https://www.repaircafe.org/"
"en/linux-repair-cafe/) on their website. And the Restart Project published "
"their own \"[End Of Windows 10 toolkit](https://therestartproject.org/end-of-"
"windows-10-toolkit-for-repair-groups/)\" to promote FOSS among repair groups "
"as a way to keep unsupported Windows devices in use."
msgstr ""
"Julija 2026, nekaj več kot eno leto po drugem spletnem seminarju, je na "
"spletni strani Konec desetke/End Of 10 navedenih več kot 85 mest in več kot "
"170 dogodkov organizacij servisnih kavarn, Linuxovih kavarn (tj. servisnih "
"kavarn, osredotočenih posebej na Linux) in podobnih organizacij, kot so IT-"
"Cafés, Technik-Cafés itd. (Ko vključite še Makerspaces, Hackerspaces, "
"Fablabs, LUG in druge pobude, ki so priskočile na pomoč, je na spletni "
"strani Konec desetke/End Of 10 skupno več kot 1180 mest in dogodkov – več o "
"tem v drugem delu.) Poleg tega Repair Café International, [organizacija, ki "
"podpira Konec desetke/End Of 10](https://endof10.org/#supporters), zdaj na "
"svoji spletni strani navaja 40 [Linux servisnih kavarn](https://www."
"repaircafe.org/en/linux-repair-cafe/). Projekt Restart je objavil svoj "
"komplet orodij »[Konec sistema Windows 10](https://therestartproject.org/end-"
"of-windows-10-toolkit-for-repair-groups/)«, da bi med skupinami za popravila "
"promoviral FOSS kot način za ohranitev uporabe nepodprtih naprav Windows."

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:56
msgid ""
"One End Of 10 contributor came up with a slogan which I feel captures this "
"connection between repair and Free & Open Source Software beautifully, "
"namely:"
msgstr ""
"Eden od sodelavcev Konca desetke/End Of 10 si je izmislil slogan, ki po "
"mojem mnenju lepo zajame to povezavo med popravilom in prosto ter "
"odprtokodno programsko opremo, in sicer:"

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:60
msgid "**\"FOSS Instead Of Toss!\"**"
msgstr "**\"FOSS namesto Toss!\"**"

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:66
msgid ""
"![Snippet of a community poster for the End Of 10 campaign. (Image from "
"Finnjan Hofmann published under a [CC BY-SA 4.0](https://creativecommons.org/"
"licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode.en) license. Redesign by Aaron Rainbolt.)](/"
"blog/images/2026-07-22-foss-instead-of-toss.png)"
msgstr ""
"![Delček plakata skupnosti za kampanjo Konec desetke/End Of 10. (Slika "
"Finnjana Hofmanna, objavljena pod licenco [CC BY-SA 4.0](https://"
"creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0/legalcode.en). Preoblikovanje: Aaron "
"Rainbolt.)](/blog/images/2026-07-22-foss-instead-of-toss.png)"

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:71
msgid "Let's Bring FOSS and Repair Communities Together"
msgstr "Združimo skupnosti FOSS in skupnosti popravil"

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:73
msgid ""
"In order to further strengthen the ties between FOSS and repair communities, "
"the Opt Green project organized three in-person workshops from December 2025 "
"to March 2026 with support from the funders UBA and BMUKN. The idea was to "
"bring together local Repair Cafés, Fablabs, Linux User Groups, and related "
"communities for a skills and information exchange. Each event took place in "
"a different part of Germany: Hannover (middle), Nürnberg (south), and Dessau "
"(east). Half of participants at each event were repair community members, "
"half FOSS enthusiasts, and some belonged to both communities."
msgstr ""
"Da bi še bolj okrepili vezi med skupnostmi FOSS in popravil, je projekt Opt "
"Green od decembra 2025 do marca 2026 s podporo financerjev UBA in BMUKN "
"organiziral tri delavnice v živo. Ideja je bila združiti lokalne servisne "
"kavarne, Fablabe, skupine uporabnikov Linuxa in sorodne skupnosti za "
"izmenjavo znanj in informacij. Vsak dogodek je potekal v drugem delu "
"Nemčije: Hannover (sredina), Nürnberg (jug) in Dessau (vzhod). Polovica "
"udeležencev vsakega dogodka je bila članov skupnosti popravil, polovica "
"navdušencev nad FOSS, nekateri pa so pripadali obema skupnostma."

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:75
msgid "In the workshops a wide range of topics were covered, such as:"
msgstr "Na delavnicah je bila obravnavana široka paleta tem, kot so:"

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:77
msgid "How can the FOSS community support Repair Cafés, and vice versa?"
msgstr "Kako lahko skupnost FOSS podpira servisne kavarne in obratno?"

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:78
msgid ""
"What are the barriers to adoption of Linux? What do new users need to "
"succeed?"
msgstr ""
"Katere so ovire za sprejetje Linuxa? Kaj potrebujejo novi uporabniki za "
"uspeh?"

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:79
msgid ""
"After installation, how much support can Repair Cafés realistically offer? "
"Would user support fit into regular opening times? Could more technical "
"problems be directed to collaborators in local FOSS groups?"
msgstr ""
"Koliko podpore lahko servisne kavarne realno ponudijo po namestitvi? Ali bi "
"uporabniška podpora ustrezala rednemu odpiralnemu času? Ali bi lahko več "
"tehničnih težav preusmerili na sodelavce v lokalnih skupinah FOSS?"

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:80
msgid ""
"How can Linux be promoted in local communities? What are the target groups? "
"How does one reach them?"
msgstr ""
"Kako lahko Linux promoviramo v lokalnih skupnostih? Katere so ciljne "
"skupine? Kako jih doseči?"

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:81
msgid ""
"What platforms are there for Repair Café volunteers to exchange tips and "
"support each other?"
msgstr ""
"Katere platforme obstajajo za prostovoljce servisnih kavarn, kjer si lahko "
"izmenjujejo nasvete in se medsebojno podpirajo?"

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:83
msgid "And more."
msgstr "In več."

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:85
msgid ""
"Before the workshops, we also held an install event for Repair Café "
"volunteers new to Linux. That way they could roll their sleeves up and get "
"some hands-on experience."
msgstr ""
"Pred delavnicami smo organizirali tudi namestitveni dogodek za prostovoljce "
"servisne kavarne, ki so bili novinci v Linuxu. Tako so si lahko zavihali "
"rokave in pridobili nekaj praktičnih izkušenj."

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:87
msgid ""
"Clearly there is not one right answer to any of the above questions, while "
"just having two days for an exchange between locally-networked groups was as "
"important as any one comment or reply. Even though there is, as always, room "
"for improvement, the feedback from these workshops from all involved was "
"overall very positive. If you live in an area with active Repair Cafés and "
"Linux User Groups I strongly recommend organizing similar cross-community "
"workshops in your town. Don't hesitate to be in touch if you want some "
"guidance!"
msgstr ""
"Očitno na nobeno od zgornjih vprašanj ni enega samega pravilnega odgovora, "
"čeprav je bilo že samo dva dni za izmenjavo med lokalno povezanimi skupinami "
"prav tako pomembno kot en sam komentar ali odgovor. Čeprav je, kot vedno, "
"prostor za izboljšave, so bili odzivi vseh vpletenih na teh delavnicah na "
"splošno zelo pozitivni. Če živite na območju z aktivnimi servisnimi "
"kavarnami in skupinami uporabnikov Linuxa, toplo priporočam organizacijo "
"podobnih medskupnostnih delavnic v vašem mestu. Če potrebujete nasvet, se ne "
"oklevajte priti v stik!"

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:89
msgid ""
"You can read the minutes from all three workshops [here](https://invent.kde."
"org/teams/eco/opt-green/-/work_items/175#note_1364833) (Hannover), [here]"
"(https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/opt-green/-/work_items/183) (Nürnberg), "
"and [here](https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/opt-green/-/"
"work_items/184#note_1446930) (Dessau). Discussions from the Repair Café "
"workshops also informed the new KDE Eco handbook \"[Opting Green: "
"Sustainable Software For Sustainable Hardware&mdash;And How Repair "
"Collectives Can Bring Free & Open Source Software To Communities](https://"
"eco.kde.org/opt-green-handbook/)\". The handbook provides an overview of "
"environmental harm driven by software and how FOSS provides a solution, "
"including many tips for organizing install and support events. Check it out!"
msgstr ""
"Zapisnike vseh treh delavnic si lahko preberete [tukaj](https://invent.kde."
"org/teams/eco/opt-green/-/work_items/175#note_1364833) (Hannover), [tukaj]"
"(https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/opt-green/-/work_items/183) (Nürnberg) in "
"[tukaj](https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/opt-green/-/"
"work_items/184#note_1446930) (Dessau). Razprave z delavnic servisnih kavarn "
"so bile podlaga tudi za nov priročnik KDE Eco \"[Opting Green: Trajnostna "
"programska oprema za trajnostno strojno opremo – in kako lahko servisne "
"kavarne prinesejo prosto in odprtokodno programsko opremo v skupnosti]"
"(https://eco.kde.org/opt-green-handbook/)\". Priročnik ponuja pregled "
"okoljske škode, ki jo povzroča programska oprema, in kako FOSS ponuja "
"rešitve, vključno s številnimi nasveti za organizacijo dogodkov za "
"namestitev in podporo. Oglejte si ga!"

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:91
msgid "After The Workshops"
msgstr "Po delavnicah"

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:93
msgid "Since March, several exciting updates have made it into our inbox."
msgstr "Od marca je v naš nabiralnik prispelo več vznemirljivih posodobitev."

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:95
msgid ""
"We learned that four repair cafe volunteers from [*Repair-Café Wendelstein*]"
"(https://www.wendelstein-evangelisch.de/repaircafe) who attended the "
"workshop have now started offering [Linux support](https://web.archive.org/"
"web/20260718105937/https://www.wendelstein-evangelisch.de/repaircafe). Also, "
"attendees from [*Reparatur Café Helmstedt*](https://reparatur-cafe-he.de/) "
"have organized two install events and one [Linux User Training](https://web."
"archive.org/web/20260721110842/https://reparatur-cafe-he.de/) in their café "
"since the workshops. The Repair Café at the neighborhood cultural center "
"[*Haus Drei*](https://haus-drei.de/) in Hamburg now holds regular Linux "
"installation workshops as well."
msgstr ""
"Izvedeli smo, da so štirje prostovoljci iz servisne kavarne Repair Café "
"Wendelstein*](https://www.wendelstein-evangelisch.de/repaircafe), ki so se "
"udeležili delavnice, začeli ponujati [podporo za Linux](https://web.archive."
"org/web/20260718105937/https://www.wendelstein-evangelisch.de/repaircafe). "
"Prav tako so udeleženci iz servisne kavarne Repair Café Helmstedt*](https://"
"reparatur-cafe-he.de/) po delavnicah v svoji kavarni organizirali dva "
"namestitvena dogodka in eno [usposabljanje za uporabnike Linuxa](https://web."
"archive.org/web/20260721110842/https://reparatur-cafe-he.de/). "
"Popravljalnica kavarna Repair Café v soseski kulturnem centru [*Haus Drei*]"
"(https://haus-drei.de/) v Hamburgu zdaj redno organizira tudi delavnice o "
"namestitvi Linuxa."

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:97
msgid ""
"What is more, [*Repair Café Hilpoltstein*](https://www.repaircafe-"
"hilpoltstein.de/), one of the groups that was already offering Linux support "
"(their website is full of helpful information), has launched a [Discourse "
"forum](https://forum.makes-hacks-hip.de/) (in German) to provide community "
"support for Repair Café volunteers. If you help out at a Repair Café and "
"want some guidance with Linux, this will be an excellent resource!"
msgstr ""
"Še več, [*Repair Café Hilpoltstein*](https://www.repaircafe-hilpoltstein."
"de/), ena od skupin, ki je že ponujala podporo za Linux (njihova spletna "
"stran je polna koristnih informacij), je ustanovila [Discourse forum]"
"(https://forum.makes-hacks-hip.de/) (v nemščini), da bi zagotovila podporo "
"skupnosti prostovoljcem servisne kavarne. Če pomagate v servisni kavarni in "
"želite nekaj nasvetov glede Linuxa, bo to odličen vir!"

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:99
msgid ""
"We also brought KDE Eco materials to the workshops in order to distribute "
"them to interested groups around Germany and Austria. So it was great to see "
"that *Repair Café Hilpoltstein* had an [info stand](https://web.archive.org/"
"web/20260718110459/https://www.repaircafe-hilpoltstein.de/blog/artikel/"
"pfingstmarkt-in-hip-neues-aus-der-offenen-werkstatt) at a local market in "
"May, featuring among other things the [\"Environmentally-Friendly Software\" "
"leaflet](https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/opt-green/-/tree/master/materials/"
"leaflets/EN/current-version) ([German version](https://invent.kde.org/teams/"
"eco/opt-green/-/tree/master/materials/leaflets/DE/current-version)) from the "
"Opt Green project."
msgstr ""
"Na delavnice smo prinesli tudi gradiva KDE Eco, da bi jih razdelili "
"zainteresiranim skupinam po Nemčiji in Avstriji. Zato je bilo super videti, "
"da je imel *Repair Café Hilpoltstein* maja na lokalni tržnici [informativno "
"stojnico](https://web.archive.org/web/20260718110459/https://www.repaircafe-"
"hilpoltstein.de/blog/artikel/pfingstmarkt-in-hip-neues-aus-der-offenen-"
"werkstatt), na kateri je bil med drugim predstavljen [letak »Okolju prijazna "
"programska oprema«](https://invent.kde.org/teams/eco/opt-green/-/tree/master/"
"materials/leaflets/EN/current-version) ([nemška različica](https://invent."
"kde.org/teams/eco/opt-green/-/tree/master/materials/leaflets/DE/current-"
"version)) iz projekta Opt Green."

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:103
msgid ""
"![Photo from the Pentecost Market in Hilpoltstein, Germany. One can see the "
"KDE Eco flyer spread across the *Repair Café Hilpoltstein* table.](/blog/"
"images/2026-07-22-hip-info-stand.jpg)"
msgstr ""
"![Fotografija z binkoštne tržnice v Hilpoltsteinu v Nemčiji. Na mizi v "
"*Repair Café Hilpoltstein* je razprostrt letak KDE Eco.](/blog/"
"images/2026-07-22-hip-info-stand.jpg)"

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:107
msgid ""
"The Repair Café workshops also led to other outreach opportunities. The "
"Hilpoltstein group organized an [info-meetup](https://floss.social/"
"@be4foss/116720438501362487) for [FOSS in Volunteer Work](https://archive."
"is/2Fnyb) in the Nürnberg region in June, with KDE Eco as a presentation "
"partner. They are planning more local outreach in the near future as well, "
"especially since Bavaria announced in June that [no new deals will be made "
"with Microsoft, at least for now](https://www.br.de/nachrichten/bayern/"
"korrektur-der-staatsregierung-vorerst-kein-deal-mit-microsoft,VLTSkXp)."
msgstr ""
"Delavnice v servisnih kavarnah so prinesle tudi druge priložnosti za "
"ozaveščanje. Skupina Hilpoltstein je junija v regiji Nürnberg organizirala "
"[informativno srečanje](https://floss.social/@be4foss/116720438501362487) za "
"[FOSS in Volunteer Work](https://archive.is/2Fnyb), predstavitveni partner "
"pa je bil KDE Eco. V bližnji prihodnosti načrtujejo tudi več lokalnega "
"ozaveščanja, še posebej, ker je Bavarska junija napovedala, da [vsaj "
"zaenkrat ne bo sklenjenih novih poslov z Microsoftom](https://www.br.de/"
"nachrichten/bayern/korrektur-der-staatsregierung-vorerst-kein-deal-mit-"
"microsoft,VLTSkXp)."

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:109
msgid ""
"FOSS and repair go together&mdash;and it is exciting to see FOSS and repair "
"communities connect and grow. I am proud of the work Opt Green did in "
"contributing to this. If there are Repair Cafés in your town or city, reach "
"out to see how you can support their work!"
msgstr ""
"FOSS in popravila gredo z roko v roki – in vznemirljivo je videti, kako se "
"skupnosti FOSS in popravil povezujejo in rastejo. Ponosen sem na delo, ki ga "
"je Opt Green opravila pri prispevanju k temu. Če so v vašem mestu ali kraju "
"servisne kavarne, se obrnite nanje in preverite, kako lahko podprete njihovo "
"delo!"

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:111
msgid ""
"Keep your eyes on this blog for the second installment about End Of 10, the "
"global campaign started by Opt Green to promote FOSS as a way to prevent e-"
"waste. As some of us in the community are saying: \"FOSS instead of toss!\""
msgstr ""
"Spremljajte ta blog za drugi del o Kocu desetke/End Of 10, globalni "
"kampanji, ki jo je začela organizacija Opt Green za promocijo FOSS kot "
"načina za preprečevanje nastajanja e-odpadkov. Kot pravimo nekateri v "
"skupnosti: \"FOSS namesto toss!\""

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:113
msgid "Starting A Linux Repair Cafe"
msgstr "Odprtje Linux servisne kavarne"

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:115
msgid ""
"If you would like to start a Repair Café in your town or city, Repair Cafe "
"International has some helpful information at the \"[Start Your Own](https://"
"www.repaircafe.org/en/join/start-your-own/)\" and \"[Linux Repair Café]"
"(https://www.repaircafe.org/linux-repair-cafe/)\" webpages. Restart Project "
"has prepared a \"[End of Windows 10: A Toolkit for Community Repair Groups]"
"(https://therestartproject.org/end-of-windows-10-toolkit-for-repair-"
"groups/)\". You may also enjoy reading up on some [strategies to getting "
"started](https://eco.kde.org/opt-green-handbook/#stage-1-gaining-experience) "
"in the Opt Green handbook."
msgstr ""
"Če želite v svojem mestu ali kraju ustanoviti servisno kavarno, vam Repair "
"Cafe International ponuja nekaj koristnih informacij na spletnih straneh "
"»[Start Your Own](https://www.repaircafe.org/en/join/start-your-own/)« in "
"»[Linux Repair Café](https://www.repaircafe.org/linux-repair-cafe/)«. "
"Projekt Restart je pripravil »[Konec sistema Windows 10: Komplet orodij za "
"skupine za popravilo v skupnosti](https://therestartproject.org/end-of-"
"windows-10-toolkit-for-repair-groups/)«. Morda vam bo všeč tudi branje "
"nekaterih [strategij za začetek](https://eco.kde.org/opt-green-handbook/"
"#stage-1-gaining-experience) v priročniku Opt Green."

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:117
msgid "When Repair Is Not Possible"
msgstr "Ko popravilo ni mogoče"

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:119
msgid ""
"When you need to buy new hardware, look into one of many Linux-supported "
"devices on the market. That way you can use the computer for as long as the "
"hardware keeps working. With devices made for Linux you will have a better "
"out-of-the-box experience too, with less tinkering and fewer workarounds "
"needed to get pesky proprietary-software components working."
msgstr ""
"Ko morate kupiti novo strojno opremo, poiščite eno od številnih naprav, ki "
"podpirajo Linux, ki so na trgu. Tako lahko računalnik uporabljate, dokler "
"strojna oprema deluje. Z napravami, izdelanimi za Linux, boste imeli tudi "
"boljšo izkušnjo takoj po namestitvi, saj boste potrebovali manj posegov in "
"manj rešitev, da bi zagnali nadležne komponente lastniške programske opreme."

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:121
msgid ""
"KDE [supporting members](https://ev.kde.org/supporting-members/) like "
"[Slimbook](https://slimbook.com/), [Kubuntu Focus](https://kfocus.org/), "
"[Tuxedo Computers](https://www.tuxedocomputers.com/), [framework](https://"
"frame.work/) all sell hardware with native Linux support. Many offer "
"hardware replacement parts and repair guides too, so you can easily swap out "
"broken pieces when needed."
msgstr ""
"KDE [podporni člani](https://ev.kde.org/supporting-members/), kot so "
"[Slimbook](https://slimbook.com/), [Kubuntu Focus](https://kfocus.org/), "
"[Tuxedo Computers](https://www.tuxedocomputers.com/) in [framework](https://"
"frame.work/), vsi prodajajo strojno opremo z izvorno podporo za Linux. Mnogi "
"ponujajo tudi nadomestne dele strojne opreme in navodili za popravilo, tako "
"da lahko po potrebi preprosto zamenjate pokvarjene dele."

#: content/blog/2026-07-22-opt-green-end-part-i-repair-cafes.md:123
msgid ""
"If you instead decide to buy a new computer with Microsoft pre-installed but "
"plan to install Linux instead, check out the [Refund 4 Freedom](https://en."
"refund4freedom.org/) initiative. Here you can learn how to get a refund for "
"that Windows license you paid for even when you did not want it."
msgstr ""
